11, 270710, 270709, 270688, 270687, 270686, 270685, 270612, 270611, 270610, 270609, 270608, 270607, 270589, 270436, 270426, 270396, 269860, 269793, 269397, 269258, 269257, 269240, 269168, 269159, 269158, 269157, 269156, 269155, 268502, 268432, 268431, 268430, 268429, 268426, 267559, 267534, 267509, 267497, 267467, 267466, 267465, 267464, 267451, 267450, 267449, 267338, 267337, 267267, 267266, 267261, 267132, 267131, 267130, 267128, 267127, 267124, 267122, 267121, 267120, 267119, 267118, 267117, 267116, 267115, 267112, 267106, 267105, 267104, 267102, 267101, 267100, 267099, 267098, 267097, 267096, 267095, 267094, 267092, 267090, 267089, 267088, 267086, 267085, 267084, 267083, 267082, 267081, 267080, 267078, 267077, 267076, 267075, 267074, 267073, 267071, 267066, 267065, 265601, 265600, 265598, 265597, 265596, 265595, 265594, 265593, 265592, 265591, 265590, 265584, 265583, 265582, 265581, 265580, 265573, 263949, 263948, 263820, 263818, 263817, 263698, 263697, 263626, 262195, 256945, 245265, 245263, 245262);
INSERT INTO `broadcast_text` (`Text`, `Text1`, `ID`, `LanguageID`, `ConditionID`, `EmotesID`, `Flags`, `ChatBubbleDurationMs`, `VoiceOverPriorityID`, `SoundKitID1`, `SoundKitID2`, `EmoteID1`, `EmoteID2`, `EmoteID3`, `EmoteDelay1`, `EmoteDelay2`, `EmoteDelay3`, `VerifiedBuild`) VALUES
('There is much to reflect on, $n.', '', 280383, 0, 0, 0, 0, 1, 1024, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 58162),
('Feels good to be back on de open air!\n\nNever felt right after we all went on strike with Cableclamp. Her contractors weren\'t payin\' any of us--her included! So she brought the Princess down. Eventually we went our own separate ways for a while.\n\nBut we be back and ready to fly! Ha ha!\n\nExcept Du\'una. She\'s afraid of de bwon\'tulak, which I don\'t blame her. \n\nWe\'re sailin\' right into stormy weathers, but Shango always watchin\' over us in de storms!', '', 279769, 0, 0, 0, 0, 1, 1024, 0, 0, 256, 1024, 0, 0, 0, 0, 58162),
('', 'You headin\' to the Siren Isle?\n\n<Du\'una grimaces around her tusks and spits.>\n\nI told Cableclamp dis is a bad omen. I\'ve heard stories about de sirens. In zandali, we call dem \"bwon\'tulak.\" Death Singers. Terrible creatures.\n\nI am blessed. I never encountered dem before in all my time flyin\' over de seas. But now we\'re headin\' for a place named after dem?\n\n<Du\'una bows and shakes her head.>\n\nMay Shango guide de winds.', 279768, 0, 0, 0, 0, 1, 1024, 0, 0, 60672, 4611, 1, 0, 0, 0, 58162),
('Why, adventure of course!\n\n<Regald chuckles deeply before he shakes his head.>\n\nAs a Lamplighter, it is our duty to guide those in need through the darkness. This expedition may not be a military operation, but it still requires protection. \n\nHallowfall cannot spare to lose many Lamplighters, but I would not allow our scholars to travel half a world away without a guiding light.', '', 279765, 0, 0, 0, 0, 1, 1024, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 58162),
('Sacred Flame guide you, friend!\n\nDo watch yourself on this island. It would seem we are not the only ones interested in this strange place.', '', 279763, 0, 0, 0, 0, 1, 1024, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 58162),
('', 'Ah, $n! You decided to make the journey after all!\n\nI am most pleased. It is good to see so many Awakened earthen stepping beyond the lands of Khaz Algar.\n\nMay curiosity guide your steps around the Isle!', 279762, 0, 0, 0, 0, 1, 1024, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 58162),
('', '<Angorla looks closely at the ring, tilting her head slightly as she examines it.>\n\nIt appears to be forged of the very same iron found around the isle. I believe the Arathi have called it \"flame-blessed iron\", but I do not see the logic in such a name. There is no properties of fire within the ore so why--\n\n<Angorla catches herself going on a professional tangent and continues.>\n\nThe craftsmanship of the circlet is quite ornate and detailed. \n\nThe sockets are intricately carved and smoothed as to resonate the power of gems set in it. It fits perfectly for those citrines you found.\n\nYou have found quite the mysterious treasure, $n.', 279761, 0, 0, 0, 0, 1, 1024, 0, 0, 60672, 3, 0, 0, 0, 0, 58162),
('Is it not an unusual convergence of coincidence that we are not the first titanforged to discover this crystal? I cannot help but query what mysteries they may have learned from this crystal.\n\nTo think we were in such close proximity to a crystal similar to this back home, but unable to approach or even study it. Our edicts simply forbade it as it was not part of them.', 'Is it not an unusual convergence of coincidence that we are not the first titanforged to discover this crystal? I cannot help but query what mysteries they may have learned from this crystal.\n\nTo think we were in such close proximity to a crystal similar to this back home, but unable to approach or even study it. Our edicts simply forbade it as it was not part of them.', 279759, 0, 0, 0, 0, 1, 1024, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 58162),
('The device you helped Bargus forge has been yielding interesting results. \n\nWith the signal stabilized by these pylons, we are able to calculate the flow of the energy patterns. They seem to be almost... sporadic. Unpredictable in nature, but not in a threatening way. \n\nIt is almost like the crystal is cautiously reaching out. But for what purposes, I cannot process.', 'The device you helped Bargus forge has been yielding interesting results. \n\nWith the signal stabilized by these pylons, we are able to calculate the flow of the energy patterns. They seem to be almost... sporadic. Unpredictable in nature, but not in a threatening way. \n\nIt is almost like the crystal is cautiously reaching out. But for what purposes, I cannot process.', 279758, 0, 0, 0, 0, 1, 1024, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 58162),
('We are collecting data to send back to the Archive and share with High Speaker Brinthe and the rest of the Council.\n\nBetween our knowledge of geological material and the Arathi\'s expertise on Beledar, there is plenty of information to process and go disseminate.', 'We are collecting data to send back to the Archive and share with High Speaker Brinthe and the rest of the Council.\n\nBetween our knowledge of geological material and the Arathi\'s expertise on Beledar, there is plenty of information to process and go disseminate.', 279757, 0, 0, 0, 0, 1, 1024, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 58162),
('', '<Dawn beams with excitement.>\n\nOf course! This will be my first time departing the shores of Khaz Algar. I can think of no better way than to venture forth from my home and see the world!\n\nI won\'t be accompanying you on the goblins air-vessel, however. With the support of Moira Bronzebeard\'s dark irons, High Speaker Brinthe has secured us an alternative route to the Siren Isle.\n\nShe called them \"mole machines.\" I am most intrigued.\n\nA few of the Awakened were not so keen to travel long-distance over the open waters so we will be departing from Gundargaz soon.\n\nI hope to see you on the island, my friend!', 279752, 0, 0, 0, 0, 1, 1024, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 58162),
('Eh, there\'s some new construction venture she\'s real excited about right now, so she didn\'t have the time to come with.\n\nWhat could be more exciting than a singin\' crystal? Whatever, she\'s missin\' out.\n\n<Skaggit shrugs and waves his hand.>', '', 279750, 0, 0, 0, 0, 1, 1024, 0, 0, 1536, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 58162),
('The name\'s Skaggit, and I\'m Galzowe\'s assistant. I lead the Greasemonkeys and am generally in charge of most ventures Monte is too busy to run.\n\nWhich is almost everything these days.\n\n<Skaggit sighs.>\n\nBein\' part of the Horde Council doesn\'t give him a lotta free time. And with his recent business in Khaz Algar lately... well, I\'m here to be his eyes and ears out in the field when he can\'t be.\n\nThe Greasemonkeys will always get the job done! Whatever and wherever it is.', '', 279748, 0, 0, 0, 0, 1, 1024, 0, 0, 1536, 0, 0, 0, 59392, 3, 58162),
('Almost nothin\', unfortunately. I put my best guys on it to see what they could dig up.\n\nThey didn\'t find much; just a few tales from Boralus. The oldest record we could find was some Kul Tiran fable or somethin\' warning us of the dangers of \'The Call\', whatever that means. \n\nCouldn\'t find any charts or nothin\'. Seems like a place most have steered clear from, but it sounds like an opportunity if ya ask me!\n\nThankfully Ricket and my ground crew gave us enough data to work with so we could find our way back.', '', 279747, 0, 0, 0, 0, 1, 1024, 0, 0, 1536, 0, 0, 0, 59392, 3, 58162),
('<Bargus\'s furious golden gaze is locked upon the cave entrance. The foul smelling green blood of the kvaldir stains his armor and weapons.>\n\nWe were not prepared for more invaders when the tempest rolled in. These... rot-flesh wretches sailed in as soon as the storm arrived.\n\nWe can hold them off here, but a few of them made it into the Vault in their initial rush.\n\nIf you\'re venturing down below, engage your defense protocols.', '', 279745, 0, 0, 0, 0, 1, 1024, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 58162),
('As soon as we saw the clouds fast rolling in, the expedition packed up what they could and headed west to clearer skies.\n\nThe rest of the Stormrangers and their rooks are serving as lightning pylons for the airships in case any storm clouds stray too far west.\n\nIt should keep the rooks happy at least!', 'As soon as we saw the clouds fast rolling in, the expedition packed up what they could and headed west to clearer skies.\n\nThe rest of the Stormrangers and their rooks are serving as lightning pylons for the airships in case any storm clouds stray too far west.\n\nIt should keep the rooks happy at least!', 279744, 0, 0, 0, 0, 1, 1024, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 58162),
('We may be few in number, but it will have to do for now!\n\nThe rest of the Stormrangers have escorted the Starchaser and Cableclamp\'s zeppelin off the isle until the tempest dies down!\n\nI am not familiar with the structural integrity of Arathi or goblin air vessels... but I am confident to presume their ships would not have survived this impact!', 'We may be few in number, but it will have to do for now!\n\nThe rest of the Stormrangers have escorted the Starchaser and Cableclamp\'s zeppelin off the isle until the tempest dies down!\n\nI am not familiar with the structural integrity of Arathi or goblin air vessels... but I am confident to presume their ships would not have survived this impact!', 279743, 0, 0, 0, 0, 1, 1024, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 58162),
('So, you decided to stay and brave the tempest?\n\nAn admirable conclusion! You would make an excellent Stormrider--or Stormranger!', 'So, you decided to stay and brave the tempest?\n\nAn admirable conclusion! You would make an excellent Stormrider--or Stormranger!', 279742, 0, 0, 0, 0, 1, 1024, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 58162),
('I didn\'t expect our journey to take us this far from home.  \n\nThen again, I don\'t think I ever had a true comprehension of what \"far from home\" really meant.\n\nI started to get a better idea when I could no longer see the Isle of Dorn behind me on the horizon.\n\nBut... we are here now and we have a job to do.', 'I didn\'t expect our journey to take us this far from home.  \n\nThen again, I don\'t think I ever had a true comprehension of what \"far from home\" really meant.\n\nI started to get a better idea when I could no longer see the Isle of Dorn behind me on the horizon.\n\nBut... we are here now and we have a job to do.', 279741, 0, 0, 0, 0, 1, 1024, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 58162),
('The goblins have informed us of the particularly violent weather patterns here on this \"Siren Isle.\" It appears the storms make many uneasy and nervous.\n\n<The Stormranger smiles gently.> \n\nAn unfortunate reception, of course. Don\'t tell them but I\'ve grown quite fond of stormy weather.', 'The goblins have informed us of the particularly violent weather patterns here on this \"Siren Isle.\" It appears the storms make many uneasy and nervous.\n\n<The Stormranger smiles gently.> \n\nAn unfortunate reception, of course. Don\'t tell them but I\'ve grown quite fond of stormy weather.', 279740, 0, 0, 0, 0, 1, 1024, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 58162),
('Isn\'t this expedition exciting?\n\nNot only is this the first time many of us earthen have ever left Khaz Algar, but this is the first officially sanctioned Stormranger mission to serve on behalf of the Council!\n\nWhen the Arathi\'s vessel, the Starchaser, first left the Isle of Dorn, the Stormward wanted to ensure our allies were properly protected on their journey.\n\nWe have much to learn on this isle, friend. Both from this crystal... and our new allies.', 'Isn\'t this expedition exciting?\n\nNot only is this the first time many of us earthen have ever left Khaz Algar, but this is the first officially sanctioned Stormranger mission to serve on behalf of the Council!\n\nWhen the Arathi\'s vessel, the Starchaser, first left the Isle of Dorn, the Stormward wanted to ensure our allies were properly protected on their journey.\n\nWe have much to learn on this isle, friend. Both from this crystal... and our new allies.', 279739, 0, 0, 0, 0, 1, 1024, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 58162),
('During my time in the Second War, I heard tale of an island so cursed that no Kul Tiran sailor worth their salt would ever venture there. I\'m pretty sure this is the same isle, so hopefully this won\'t be a \'set out and never return\' scenario.\n\nStill it begs the question; what was so scary about this island that ingrained itself in generations of Kul Tiran sailors? Hopefully we don\'t find out- there\'s no way the hazard pay would cover somethin\' like that.\n\n<Krazz pauses.>\n\nActually, with Gazlowe\'s new \'Hazard Pay Initiative\' maybe it would. Back in my day we never would\'ve had coverage like this! \n\n<Krazz scrunches up his nose.>\n\nStill, if it is in favor of new expeditions... well, I can\'t fault Gazlowe\'s deep pockets, eh?', '', 279729, 0, 0, 0, 0, 1, 1024, 0, 0, 256, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 58162),
('Honestly I ain\'t ever heard of it before now. But I haven\'t been in the air as long as Krazz or some of the other zeppelin captains.\n\n<Fergus shrugs.>\n\nSeems like a perfect time for new stories to me!', '', 279726, 0, 0, 0, 0, 1, 1024, 0, 0, 256, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 58162),
('', 'Siren Isle?\n\nWell, I never heard of it referred to as that, but it makes sense--what with the stories of the sirens and all. \n\nMy cousin Krooz used to tell me stories of all the places she used to smuggle to. \n\nAlways told me of this one spooky place with nasty storms around it and even nastier singin\' ladies!\n\nApparently her buddies in Freehold are scared hatless of the place--so much that she started avoidin\' it outta principle. And, well, for business reasons.\n\nOf course, I didn\'t clue in that this was the place until I was already in Dornogal. Go figure, huh?', 279724, 0, 0, 0, 0, 1, 1024, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 58162),
('It\'s good to be serve\'n under Captain Krazz again, though I will say I\'m equally excited to be able to work with Sky-Captain Cableclamp! Her laid back attitude is legendary.\n\nI\'m glad she was able to find work after the Purple Princess\'s zeppelin circuit from Brill to Grom\'gol was, uh, \'decommissioned\'.', '', 279722, 0, 0, 0, 0, 1, 1024, 0, 0, 256, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 58162),
('<Bargus is focused on the anvil in front of him. After a moment, he glances up from his work and offers you a firm nod and a friendly smile.>\n\nIt is good to see more Ordinants awakening from within the machine.\n\nMay your forge burn bright and your hammer ring true.', '', 279721, 0, 0, 0, 0, 1, 1024, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 58162),
('Normally, I would default to \"following my designation\" or \"going where the Stoneward wills\" as a response but... that would be partially inaccurate. \n\nDawn did not enact authoritative protocols when recruiting my assistance. It was an offer not a command.\n\nAs an Ordinant, I have always put the earthen first. I was sworn to fortify, arm, and if need be, defend other earthen designations. It was never a choice. It was simply my charge.\n\nBut since my recent awakening, I have been uncertain as to what awaits me. Uncertain as to my purpose.\n\nDawn promised this expedition would make use of my specified configurations. As long as I have a forge, I am content to follow even if it means leaving the shores of Khaz Algar.', '', 279719, 0, 0, 0, 0, 1, 1024, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 58162),
('It is an on-going process. The device we forged is still attuned to the crystal\'s energy signal. We are slowly processing the information it is feeding us.\n\nThe vaults defenses prevent us from establishing a research station inside, so we have opted to learn what we can on the surface.\n\nI do query about those iron vrykul shades that attacked us. They didn\'t appear to be spirits but rather memories from another time. \n\nBut whose memories, I cannot decipher. The vrykul themselves? The crystal perhaps?\n\nWe have much to learn from this island and the secrets it contains.', '', 279716, 0, 0, 0, 0, 1, 1024, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 58162),
('I have formulated more queries than answers, unfortunately.\n\nWhen we embarked on this journey, we had hoped to learn more about this crystal. What we had not expected was to find other titanforged connected to it.\n\nSome of our scouts found additional titanforged ruins around the island. I am left wondering just how large this iron vrykul settlement was... \n\nWhat was their purpose was here? What compelled them to protect this crystal?\n\nAnd why did their titanforged edicts not prevent them from approaching the crystal like ours did with Beledar?\n\nMore queries. Fewer answers.', '', 279714, 0, 0, 0, 0, 1, 1024, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 58162),
('My knowledge of this particular location is limited. I am unfamiliar with anything beyond the shores of Khaz Algar.\n\nFrom the whisperings of the goblins here, I am to presume that this place instills some sort of \"unease\" in certain individuals. \n\nIt would seen superstition plays a significant factor in the history of this place.\n\nA history I have yet to learn.', '', 279713, 0, 0, 0, 0, 1, 1024, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 58162),
('I will admit I was skeptical when I heard there was a \"singing crystal\" on an island so far from Hallowfall. \n\nBeledar, for all we knew, was unlike anything we had ever seen. We had crossed the world to find it!\n\nAnd yet... we have this. A sister to our own beloved star. \n\nWe\'ve named it Lorandel. It means \"Voice of the Sea.\"', 'I will admit I was skeptical when I heard there was a \"singing crystal\" on an island so far from Hallowfall. \n\nBeledar, for all we knew, was unlike anything we had ever seen. We had crossed the world to find it!\n\nAnd yet... we have this. A sister to our own beloved star. \n\nWe\'ve named it Lorandel. It means \"Voice of the Sea.\"', 279709, 0, 0, 0, 0, 1, 1024, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 58162),
('It has been many years since I have seen the open skies. I never thought I\'d leave the confines of Hallowfall--let alone venture this far out of Khaz Algar.\n\nBut when I heard rumors of another crystal--one that sings like Beledar--I and so many others had to see it for ourselves!\n\nLorandel may not have been a star of prophecy like Beledar, but it is not something we can ignore.\n \nWe have much to learn from this sister star.', 'It has been many years since I have seen the open skies. I never thought I\'d leave the confines of Hallowfall--let alone venture this far out of Khaz Algar.\n\nBut when I heard rumors of another crystal--one that sings like Beledar--I and so many others had to see it for ourselves!\n\nLorandel may not have been a star of prophecy like Beledar, but it is not something we can ignore.\n \nWe have much to learn from this sister star.', 279705, 0, 0, 0, 0, 1, 1024, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 58162),
('Man, am I glad to be back in the air again! Well, I guess \'consulting\' is more the correct term. \n\nFor a sea voyage as long this, it only makes sense they pulled a seasoned pilot like myself out of retirement! I did even fly a Warchief or two into battle after all.\n\nI hear this island has a lotta storms or somethin\'. Ah, it reminds me of my days back in the Second War, ferry\'n troops around...\n\n<Captain Kazz grins widely.>\n\nAnyway, Cableclamp is a great captain, so rest assured she\'ll getcha where ya need to go.', '', 279704, 0, 0, 0, 0, 1, 1024, 0, 0, 256, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 58162),
('Is it true what the earthen said? Is there really a chamber under our feet with another facet?\n\nTo think these iron vrykul once revered or venerated Lorandel as we do Beledar. Who would have guessed the similarities in our cultures... our beliefs!\n\nFascinating!', 'Is it true what the earthen said? Is there really a chamber under our feet with another facet?\n\nTo think these iron vrykul once revered or venerated Lorandel as we do Beledar. Who would have guessed the similarities in our cultures... our beliefs!\n\nFascinating!', 279703, 0, 0, 0, 0, 1, 1024, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 58162),
('I spent the last few years studying Beledar within the halls of the Priory.\n\nOn occasion, we would fly our airships as close as we could to it to observe it up close for study... but never up close like this. \n\nTo think that this crystal is just like our beloved Beledar. It is truly a splendor to behold.', 'I spent the last few years studying Beledar within the halls of the Priory.\n\nOn occasion, we would fly our airships as close as we could to it to observe it up close for study... but never up close like this. \n\nTo think that this crystal is just like our beloved Beledar. It is truly a splendor to behold.', 279702, 0, 0, 0, 0, 1, 1024, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 58162),
('The Sacredites, or sacred scholars if you will, are those dedicated to studying the Sacred Flame through unique discipline or craft. \n\nSome study the flame through scripture and prayer. \n\nOthers study it from a more practical,  hands-on perspective by working it into their craft whether it be weapons, armaments or technology.\n\nI\'ve chosen to study the key flames and the smaller fragments we use to fuel them. We call them radiant remnants.\n\nI brought a crate of them to see if they share any properties with Lorandel as they do with Beledar.', 'The Sacredites, or sacred scholars if you will, are those dedicated to studying the Sacred Flame through unique discipline or craft. \n\nSome study the flame through scripture and prayer. \n\nOthers study it from a more practical,  hands-on perspective by working it into their craft whether it be weapons, armaments or technology.\n\nI\'ve chosen to study the key flames and the smaller fragments we use to fuel them. We call them radiant remnants.\n\nI brought a crate of them to see if they share any properties with Lorandel as they do with Beledar.', 279700, 0, 0, 0, 0, 1, 1024, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 58162),
('Sacred Flame guide you, $n!\n\nAs you can no doubt see, we\'ve got quite the operation underway.\n\nI am confident that the Starchaser has been adequately stocked with all necessary provisions, tools and whatever else we may need.\n\nYou are welcome to browse my excess inventory. Perhaps you would be willing to trade for some of that flame-blessed iron I\'ve seen around the camp?', 'Sacred Flame guide you, $n!\n\nAs you can no doubt see, we\'ve got quite the operation underway.\n\nI am confident that the Starchaser has been adequately stocked with all necessary provisions, tools and whatever else we may need.\n\nYou are welcome to browse my excess inventory. Perhaps you would be willing to trade for some of that flame-blessed iron I\'ve seen around the camp?', 279696, 0, 0, 0, 0, 1, 1024, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 58162),
('When I heard the young prince tellin\' High Speaker Brinthe about our mole machines, I knew it was only a matter o\' time before the Machine Speakers got curious. \n\nWhen Dagran commissioned our help for Dawn\'s expedition, I was keen to be o\' service!\n\nI just wish we had gone somewhere less... wet.', 'When I heard the young prince tellin\' High Speaker Brinthe about our mole machines, I knew it was only a matter o\' time before the Machine Speakers got curious. \n\nWhen Dagran commissioned our help for Dawn\'s expedition, I was keen to be o\' service!\n\nI just wish we had gone somewhere less... wet.', 279694, 0, 0, 0, 0, 1, 1024, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 58162),
('Welcome, friend.\n\nIt may not be much, but feel free to rest here as long as you need. \n\nWe stocked the Starchaser with an abundance of supplies. Whether it be drink or food, we have plenty to share.', 'Welcome, friend.\n\nIt may not be much, but feel free to rest here as long as you need. \n\nWe stocked the Starchaser with an abundance of supplies. Whether it be drink or food, we have plenty to share.', 279605, 0, 0, 0, 0, 1, 1024, 0, 0, 256, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 58162),
('Have you lost something important? I can return it. \n\nFor a price.', '', 279572, 0, 0, 0, 0, 1, 1024, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 58162),
('This is a most excellent space for sparring.', 'This is a most excellent space for sparring.', 279478, 0, 0, 1, 0, 1, 1024, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 58162),
('', 'Jack is nice. He help Skitter. Holds big umbrella to protect from rain.\n\nMe no want crown to go out!', 279467, 0, 0, 0, 0, 1, 1024, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 58162),
('', 'Hey there, $p! Things are pretty different than they were back at Lightspark. I\'m learning what it means to be a captain thanks to you, and it sure helps to see how Lancekat does things before I officially take the role.\n\nSophietta will serve as my lieutenant, and Edwyn will be the ship\'s engineer. At this stage, I\'d say things are going well. I do worry about Sophietta and Edwyn getting along, considering their history, but they\'ve both been responsible and decent so far.\n\nI think we\'re going to have a bright future together as a crew when we get our ship!', 279371, 0, 0, 0, 0, 1, 1024, 0, 0, 256, 256, 0, 0, 53248, 7, 58162),
('', 'Nice to see you, $p. Things have been interesting here on the Siren Isle, and so far Edwyn hasn\'t been too difficult to work with. He definitely knows his stuff, but there are times his ego can get in the way.\n\nBut as lieutenant, it\'s my job to support him, so that\'s what I do. I\'m also specifically responsible for navigation and for the crew. And that part is going well, if I say so myself. \n\nBut it still helps to see how Lancekat\'s crew works. They clearly trust her and work well together, so you can bet I\'m taking notes!', 279370, 0, 0, 0, 0, 1, 1024, 0, 0, 256, 256, 0, 0, 53248, 7, 58162),
('It\'s humbling, $p, being a future chief engineer when I know I would have made a fine captain. I can\'t say I appreciate your meddling, but at least I\'m not reporting to Sophietta!\n\nThat said, here I am, and I have the choice whether to take this experience in stride and focus on my next adventure or sulk about what could have been. That won\'t do me or our people any good, so I\'m focusing on learning all I can from Lancekat\'s crew to be the best engineer I can.\n\nAlong with keeping the ship in peak condition, it also falls to me to ensure we\'re well-supplied and have what we need. A real challenge of organization and logistics, but I\'m getting the hang of it.', '', 279368, 0, 0, 0, 0, 1, 1024, 0, 0, 256, 256, 0, 0, 53248, 7, 58162),
('Good to see you, $p! I\'m here to shadow Sky-Captain Lancekat with Jenae and Sophietta. We\'re all learning a lot, and what I\'m learning will really help when I captain my own airship soon.\n\nThanks for your role in that by the way! I knew I\'d make the best captain, but Fynch wasn\'t sure who to choose until you spoke with him.\n\nI wonder how long it\'ll be before the new recruits are getting sent out to learn from me, just like we\'re learning from Lancekat now? Whenever it happens, I\'ll teach them what they need to know.', '', 279367, 0, 0, 0, 0, 1, 1024, 0, 0, 256, 256, 0, 0, 53248, 7, 58162),
('', 'Hello again, $p! To say I have had many interesting experiences since we last met would be an understatement. The Siren Isle has had perils we were not expecting.\n\nSo, it\'s been a blessing that we\'re here observing Sky-Captain Lancekat and her crew do what they do best.\n\nAs lieutenant, I\'ll be responsible for the ship\'s navigation and for managing the crew. It\'s been helpful on both fronts to see how tasks are handled on the Starchaser. The crew and officers have been serving together for years and really know how to get the most out of one another.\n\nI hope we can serve the people of Hallowfall just as well when we get our ship!', 279366, 0, 0, 0, 0, 1, 1024, 0, 0, 256, 256, 0, 0, 53248, 7, 58162),
('', '$p, it\'s good to see you! I\'m working to become a Chief Engineer, so my role is making sure the ship is functioning optimally and is kept in good repair. I also make sure the crew has everything they need. \n\nWhile I wanted to be captain, I am enjoying the work.\n\nThings are usually straightforward enough. But I find myself navigating challenging dynamics at times. When Edwyn and I disagree, I have to be careful how I approach him. If he feels I\'m trying to undercut him, he can get reactive.\n\nI don\'t want us to go on the wrong course of action because of a power struggle I never meant to have. So it\'s good to see how Lancekat\'s crew works together as a model.', 279365, 0, 0, 0, 0, 1, 1024, 0, 0, 256, 256, 0, 0, 53248, 7, 58162),
('', 'Thank you for your help at Lightspark, $p! While Edwyn and Jenae each have their own unique strengths, I\'m grateful that you helped Fynch see I should be selected as our future captain.\n\nIt\'s been really good to serve here under Sky-Captain Lancekat. I\'ve learned a great deal of practical, day-to-day knowledge you don\'t get at the Sky Academy. How to motivate a crew, ensure unpopular orders are followed, and project confidence in light of unexpected problems. \n\nI\'m quite grateful that Edwyn, Jenae, and I were sent on this expedition to learn under her!', 279363, 0, 0, 0, 0, 1, 1024, 0, 0, 256, 256, 0, 0, 53248, 7, 58162),
('', 'I\'m pleased to come here aboard the Starchaser! I\'ll be serving as Sophietta\'s chief engineer soon, and while we learned a great deal from Instructor Morgaen, spending time with an experienced crew gives me a chance to learn from their mistakes--so I can avoid repeating them.\n\nThere\'s a lot to manage as Chief Engineer. It will be my job to make sure our ship is properly provisioned and fully functional.\n\nHonestly, I\'ve been more worried about how Sophietta and Edwyn get along after he tried to sabotage her work. But so far it seems like we\'ve all accepted our positions and are working well together.', 279349, 0, 0, 0, 0, 1, 1024, 0, 0, 256, 256, 0, 0, 53248, 7, 58162),
('I\'ll admit I was shocked when Sophietta outperformed me at Lightspark. I thought it had to be a fluke. But, more likely it was not and she\'s even more capable than I.\n\nSeeing how Sky-Captain Lancekat and her crew work though, I\'ve set that question aside. The question I ask now is, as a future lieutenant, what can I learn in my current position and how can I continue to improve? I\'m responsible for navigation and the crew, and I approach these duties with diligence and dedication. \n\nPerhaps someday I\'ll become a captain, or perhaps not. But now that I\'ve changed my approach and goals, I\'ll always be a better officer than I was yesterday.', '', 279348, 0, 0, 0, 0, 1, 1024, 0, 0, 256, 256, 0, 0, 53248, 7, 58162),
('', 'I\'m here because I was selected as the next potential Arathi airship captain. I worked hard to get where I am, but I also know things could have gone differently. I want to take care of my crew and serve the people of Hallowfall with excellence.\n\nAnd serving under Sky-Captain Lancekat is helping me achieve that goal. I\'ve learned a great deal of practical, day-to-day knowledge you don\'t get at Lightspark. Like how to motivate a crew, how to ensure unpopular orders are followed, and how to project confidence in light of unexpected problems. \n\nI\'m quite grateful that Edwyn, Jenae and I were sent on this expedition to learn under her.', 279347, 0, 0, 0, 0, 1, 1024, 0, 0, 256, 256, 0, 0, 53248, 7, 58162),
('', 'We have processed the mistakes of our predecessors. \n\nToday is a new day in the Ringing Deeps.', 279289, 0, 0, 1, 0, 1, 1024, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 58162),
('Interested in parting with some of that ore you\'ve found from around the isle? I\'m looking to acquire... exotic goods if you\'re looking to sell.', '', 279260, 0, 0, 0, 0, 1, 1024, 0, 0, 60672, 3, 0, 0, 0, 0, 58162),
('Ever since operations have resumed in the Ringing Deeps, Steelvein has been keeping his eyes open for... future business ventures. \n\nI am here to assess and evaluate the potential of this \"Siren Isle\" and what it has to offer the earthen.\n\nShould you be interested in parting with any of the iron you find here, I will gladly trade with you.', '', 279256, 0, 0, 0, 0, 1, 1024, 0, 0, 60672, 3, 0, 0, 0, 0, 58162),
('<The Trade gives you a subtle nod as he speaks quietly to you.>\n\nSteelvein sends his regards, $n. \n\nInterested in trading some of that flame-blessed ore you\'ve found?', '', 279251, 0, 0, 0, 0, 1, 1024, 0, 0, 60672, 3, 0, 0, 0, 0, 58162),
('What can I do for ya? Ya got a special order?', '', 279200, 0, 0, 0, 0, 1, 1024, 0, 0, 256, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 58162),
('Food, huh? Yeah I think I got-\n\n<A impatient snapdragon snaps its jaws at Zexel\'s ankle.>\n\nWhoa, whoa! Wait ya turn buddy.\n\n<Zexel taps on the ground in front of its snout with his stick, and the snapdragon pulls back slightly with an irritated hiss.>\n\nHere, take this meat. My buddy Blinky over there cooked it up. It\'s meat marinated overnight in Kaja\'cola! \n\nNot only is it tasty, but it should also help the lil\' guy get some energy back. These guys seem to love it, so I\'m sure yours will too.\n\nEr, don\'t mind the color. It\'s safe to consume... mostly.', '', 279044, 0, 0, 0, 0, 1, 1024, 0, 0, 256, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 58162),
('<A muffled voice shouts from inside the machine.>\n\nAre ye daft? Have ye seen the size of those crabs out there? No chance!\n\nYe should have evacuated with the airship crews when you had the chance!\n\nWe\'re not goin\' anywhere until the storm\'s calmed down!', '', 279025, 0, 0, 0, 1, 1, 1024, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 58162),
('<The mole machine\'s hatches are sealed shut. Over the roar of the storm, you can hear voices inside the machine.>', '', 279023, 0, 0, 0, 1, 1, 1024, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 58162),
('', 'The isle? Honestly, it\'s pretty spooky if ya ask me.\n\nWhen my crew and I found it, the whole island felt so... still. Like it was wait\'n for somethin\'. I mean, sure there was a storm come\'n in but the level of calm just felt unnatural. I dunno how else to explain it.\n\n<Ricket shivers and rubs her arm.>\n\nBut hey, it\'s better now that you\'re here!', 278892, 0, 0, 0, 0, 1, 1024, 0, 0, 256, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 58162),
('The readings from this facet are identical to the ones on the surface. If my assumptions are correct, it would appear to be part of the same structure!\n\n<Bargus looks up and around at the surrounding vault.>\n\nI can\'t help but theorize on the true proportions of this crystal. I wonder if it is closer to Beledar in size...', '', 278826, 0, 0, 0, 0, 1, 1024, 0, 0, 60672, 3, 0, 0, 0, 0, 58162),
('Just because I work for Stormwind Intelligence doesn\'t mean everything I do is for the Alliance. These goblins are getting mixed up in some shady stuff. Someone has to look out for them.', '', 278819, 0, 0, 0, 0, 1, 1024, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 58162),
('', 'Captain Lancekat said we couldn\'t bring any lynx. I guess they make her sneeze a lot?\n\nBut I\'m glad I found Spots! He\'s my best friend.\n\n<Aellia suddenly looks worried.>\n\nPlease don\'t tell her about Spots! I don\'t want to have to get rid of him. What if he starts to cry again?', 278807, 0, 0, 0, 0, 1, 1024, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 58162),
('', 'I hid in a crate!\n\n<Aellia looks very proud of herself.>\n\nSygfraed told us a story about a hero that did that once. \n\nAlso Keth triple-catty-challenged me to do it! I couldn\'t say no to a triple-catty-challenge. \n\nThat\'s like, the biggest challenge there is!', 278786, 0, 0, 0, 0, 1, 1024, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 58162),
('', 'Oh! You\'re the nice outlander that came to play with us!\n\nI didn\'t recognize you right away!\n\nWe\'ve had a lot of outlanders come and play with us lately. It\'s the best!', 278785, 0, 0, 0, 0, 1, 1024, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 58162),
('', '<Aellia scrunches up her nose.>\n\nWhat\'s a wyvern? \n\nOh, you mean Spots? He\'s a flying lynx! He\'s way cooler than the ones back in Mereldar. \n\nI didn\'t know there were other kinds of lynx until I found him wet and crying under a tree the first night we got here. \n\nI wonder if his tail will get short when he\'s older?', 278784, 0, 0, 0, 0, 1, 1024, 0, 0, 256, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 58162),
('', 'Hello! Wow, you look super strong. \n\nDid you come to explore the island too?', 278776, 0, 0, 0, 0, 1, 1024, 0, 0, 256, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 58162),
('Oh sure, make the youngest brother carry everything. \n\n<Kenny grumbles.>\n\nWhadda ya want?', '', 278513, 0, 0, 0, 0, 1, 1024, 0, 0, 256, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 58162),
('Man, the wind currents on this island sure are strong. I got battered to pieces when I tried the Go-Pack.\n\nMakes me sick just thinkin\' about it.\n\n<Benny suddenly looks nauseous.>\n\nI think it\'s better if I, uh, just stay on the ground.', '', 278512, 0, 0, 0, 0, 1, 1024, 0, 0, 256, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 58162),
('', 'Have you seen my twin around? I\'m worried he\'s get\'n in trouble again. \n\nHe\'s probably off try\'n to impress someone with his \"fearlessness.\"\n\n<Jenny rolls her eyes.>\n\nBrothers, am I right?', 278511, 0, 0, 0, 0, 1, 1024, 0, 0, 256, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 58162),
('<Skaggit\'s raises his brow a bit as he looks up at you.>\n\nNo kidding... you\'ve heard of this place? Is it as bad as they say? Ricket said her crew was on edge the whole time!\n\nI met a tidesage at Stonelight Rest last week. He told me that nuthin\' good comes from that place.\n\n\"If the Siren\'s Call don\'t lure you to your death, the storms will,\" he said.\n\nMakes ya wonder what\'s lurkin\' around on the isle, don\'t it?', '', 278447, 0, 0, 0, 0, 1, 1024, 0, 0, 256, 0, 0, 0, 59392, 3, 58162),
('Of course you haven\'t--no one has! \n\nWell, unless you\'re from Boralus, of course. \n\nAccording to the Kul Tirans, this \"Siren Isle\" is a place of legend and myth. Lots of stories and old sea-tales, all of them real spooky like. \n\nSome nasty storms too!', '', 278427, 0, 0, 0, 0, 1, 1024, 0, 0, 256, 0, 0, 0, 59392, 3, 58162),
('Wouldn\'t you and half of Khaz Algar want to know! \n\nFirst the Arathi and earthen are all askin\' about it, then next thing you know, they\'re heading off in their airships and mole machines! \n\nOh, if I still had my rocket drill contacts, I betcha I coulda gotten us there faster!\n\nBut fine, ya wanna know? \n\nWe\'re headin\' to the Siren Isle. Ever heard of it?', '', 278425, 0, 0, 0, 0, 1, 1024, 0, 0, 1536, 0, 0, 0, 59392, 3, 58162),
('', '<Angorla examines the cracked shard closely.>\n\nIt would appear as if there is some sort of energy signature within the inner matrix of this shard--fascinating! \n\nCare to assist me in examining its inner workings? Or would you prefer to document and take notes while we work?', 278371, 0, 0, 0, 0, 1, 1024, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 58162),
('<Marmaduke looks at you longingly.>', '', 278296, 0, 0, 0, 0, 1, 1024, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 58162),
('', 'Stabilization complete. The crystals inner matrices begin humming with power!', 278277, 0, 0, 0, 68, 1, 1024, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 58162),
('<Soweezi looks at you in silence for a few seconds, then rubs his eyes with his fingers.> \n\nLook. Friend. Buddy. Pal.\n\nPart of relaxing at the beach is not asking so many questions. You ever hear the phrase, \"Just \'cus you\'re right, doesn\'t make you right\"? \n\nSure, it\'s dangerous. But does that mean I should be sharing a shell with the nearest mollusk whenever the waves get a little high? Nah, buddy. Just go with the flow and everything will work out.\n\n<Soweezi gives you a wink and goes back to sipping on a glass of cold Kaja\'Cola.>', '', 278273, 0, 0, 0, 0, 1, 1024, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 58162),
('Not if you got these pretty rocks, right? \n\n<Soweezi sifts through his pocket and then holds up a chunk of Flame-Blessed Iron between two fingers.> \n\nThrow these at anything that comes near ya and they\'ll kindly buzz off.\n\nPretty great, huh?', '', 278271, 0, 0, 0, 0, 1, 1024, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 58162),
('I\'m just a goblin enjoying the thirsty land my friend. I go by Soweezi.\n\nYou should kick back and go lay down in the sand. The sun ain\'t gonna soak itself.', '', 278269, 0, 0, 0, 0, 1, 1024, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 58162),
('', 'While Bargus repairs the outer chassis, let us take a closer look at the destabilized matrices in this fractured crystal, shall we?', 278267, 0, 0, 0, 68, 1, 1024, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 58162),
('Aayyy, wussup!', '', 278266, 0, 0, 0, 0, 1, 1024, 0, 0, 60672, 3, 0, 0, 0, 0, 58162),
('<Marmaduke looks at you expectantly.>', '', 278176, 0, 0, 0, 0, 1, 1024, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 58162),
('But...I do admire it.', '', 278169, 0, 0, 0, 70, 1, 1024, 69734656, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 58162),
('', 'my path is here.', 278167, 0, 0, 0, 70, 1, 1024, 0, 69734400, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 58162),
('You owe it to them to face the elders by their side.', '', 278164, 0, 0, 0, 70, 1, 1024, 69734144, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 58162),
('', '<sighs quietly>', 278163, 0, 0, 0, 70, 1, 1024, 0, 69733888, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 58162),
('but we cannot break the haranir\'s traditions any longer.', '', 278162, 0, 0, 0, 70, 1, 1024, 69733632, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 58162),
('', 'how can we not answer?', 278160, 0, 0, 0, 70, 1, 1024, 0, 69733376, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 58162),
('Coming here, revealing ourselves to the mortals, getting caught in their affairs.', '', 278158, 0, 0, 0, 70, 1, 1024, 69733120, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 58162),
('', 'Where are the others?', 278157, 0, 0, 0, 70, 1, 1024, 0, 69732864, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 58162),
('', 'Check back here anytime you need the Go-Pack.', 278029, 0, 0, 5, 0, 1, 1024, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 58162),
('<The skeletal remains sits slumped against the rocks. Its ribcage and legs are shattered and crushed by something heavy.\n\nTheir outstretched hand sits empty as if it once clutched something.>', '', 278010, 0, 0, 0, 0, 1, 1024, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 58162),
('', 'Nixx? \n\n<Eirana gives you a bashful smile.>\n\nHe\'s very sweet, and clearly loves working on zeppelins. \n\nI haven\'t had anyone listen to my engineering designs with such rapt attention before let alone discuss them with me at length after.\n\nYou should see the way his ears perk up if I ask him questions about his designs!\n\n<Eirana chuckles as she glances at Nixx.>\n\nI\'ve grown fond of his daily visits.', 278008, 0, 0, 0, 0, 1, 1024, 0, 0, 6144, 256, 0, 0, 0, 0, 58162),
('', 'Oh yes! Nixx has been very patient with my questions... and kind in his answers.\n\nIt sounds like goblins often use less... methodical means to create, repair, and maintain their zeppelins than we do our airships, but through talking to him I\'ve realized the ingenuity of their processes. Nixx\'s resourcefulness is nothing short of admirable.\n\nHe has also expressed how...\n\n<Eirana glances across the bay with concern.>\n\n...volatile their zeppelins can be. Hopefully that\'s not anything to worry about.', 278007, 0, 0, 0, 0, 1, 1024, 0, 0, 256, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 58162),
('', 'This has been a fascinating opportunity! I hadn\'t encountered a goblin until I started talking to Nixx, let alone seen one of their airships -er, I believe he called it something else. A... zeppelin, I think?\n\n<Eirana chuckles.>\n\nI love the face they\'ve sewn on the front of the zeppelin. It gives a certain character to their zeppelins that our airships don\'t have.', 278004, 0, 0, 0, 0, 1, 1024, 0, 0, 256, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 58162),
('<Nixx catches your knowing gaze.>\n\nW-what? Wait-no, it ain\'t like that!\n\nEr, well....maybe it is. So what? A guy can appreciate how brilliant his fellow engineer is, can\'t he?\n\n<He clears his throat, his cheeks darkening.>\n\nBesides, she\'s amazing. I ain\'t ever talked to anyone work\'n on an airship like that, and she sure knows her stuff. \n\n<Nixx let\'s out another wistful sigh.>\n\nMaybe I could give\'er a tour of our zeppelin sometime.', '', 278003, 0, 0, 0, 0, 1, 1024, 0, 0, 256, 6144, 0, 0, 0, 0, 58162),
('Have ya seen the airships they got over here? They\'re... incredible, honestly. For airships this well engineered, their engineers are clearly top notch!\n\n<The Goblin Zeppelin Engineer\'s eyes flit over to Eirana and he sighs wistfully.>', '', 277999, 0, 0, 0, 0, 1, 1024, 0, 0, 256, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 58162),
('<An anvil rests before you.>', '', 277982, 0, 0, 0, 0, 1, 1024, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 58162),
('<A great forge stands before you.>', '', 277979, 0, 0, 0, 0, 1, 1024, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 58162),
('<As motes of light dance around the stone altar, a strange, melodic hum seems to call you forward. The call seems to emanate from both within the crystal-dotted tablet and the rock beneath your feet.\n\nA faint, hand-shaped divot has been worn into the stone surrounding the lowest crystal on the tablet. Above this crystal, etched words read:\n\nThe Song of Cyrce.>', '', 277823, 0, 0, 0, 0, 1, 1024, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 58162),
('', 'A journal? How fascinating. Yes, I would be happy to take a look, though my knowledge of the younger races is quite... limited.\n\n<Alta studies the pages for a long while.>\n\nWhat a perplexing story. Does it not seem illogical to leave the others behind given their directive? Perhaps someone didn\'t want the records of this crew to be found.\n\nAnd to disappear so suddenly. I can\'t say that I have ever heard of such a feat.\n\n<Alta gingerly hands the worn pages back to you with a sad smile.>\n\nI am afraid I have no answers for you--only more questions.\n\nI hope you are able to find the answers you seek.', 277816, 0, 0, 0, 0, 1, 1024, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 58162),
('', 'Well met, $p. Do you have a query?', 277815, 0, 0, 0, 0, 1, 1024, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 58162),
('', '<Skitter eyes the pages warily.>\n\nI not understand. But I smell...\n\n<Skitter leans over the pages and sniffs them.>\n\nSmells of... human and salt. Dirt and cave too.\n\n<Skitter\'s brows furrow.>\n\nBut also smells of... death.\n\n<Skitter shies away from the pages.>\n\nI no like. Please take away!', 277812, 0, 0, 0, 0, 1, 1024, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 58162),
('', 'Ricket grins wickedly.', 277811, 0, 0, 574, 0, 1, 1024, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 58162),
('', 'Oh? A mystery you say? Sure, I\'ll take a look. Give \'em here, hon.\n\n<Ricket gently takes the pages you collected and thumbs through them.>\n\nWell, that\'s interestin\'. Sound\'s like they lost a boat in one of the storms. I wonder if there\'s any treasure in the wreckage...\n\n<Ricket hands you back the papers with a shrug.>\n\nHonestly, I dunno. Sounds like they weren\'t as prepared as we were. The bit about the forest is spooky but... not as spooky as those guys just straight disappearin\'.\n\n<Ricket looks around nervously.>\n\nSay, you don\'t think that will happen to us... right?', 277809, 0, 0, 0, 0, 1, 1024, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 58162),
('Look, I heard they evolved from wolves or somthin\'. Means they should be easy to train... like dogs, right?\n\nWell they ain\'t! \n\n<Zexel flinches as an impatient snapdragon snaps its salivating jaws at him. He swallows nervously.>\n\nThey sure are food motivated though.', '', 277761, 0, 0, 0, 0, 1, 1024, 0, 0, 2560, 4612, 1, 0, 59392, 3, 58162),
('\"Train snapdragons,\" they said. \"It\'ll be easy!\" they said.\n\nDoes any part of this look easy to you?\n\nDo you have any idea what their bite can do to a guy?', '', 277751, 0, 0, 0, 0, 1, 1024, 0, 0, 256, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 58162),
('He\'s broken audio playback, but just temporarily', '', 277737, 0, 0, 5, 102, 0, 1536, 69568256, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 58162),
('', 'My broiler is not the best choice. Sally has much better gear to help with this problem.', 277537, 0, 0, 5, 0, 0, 1024, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 58162),
('Oh, I sell bits and bobs to all kinds of creatures like yourself. \n\nI\'d like to think of my service as repayment to the world for showing me the wonders it has. What better way to express gratitude than to share my wonders with others?\n\nSpeaking of, I couldn\'t help but notice what you and your band of misfits over there were doing. Those yellow crystals seem like quite the curiosity. If I stumble on any, I\'ll sell them to you for cheap.\n\n<He gives a slow, reassuring wink.>', '', 277513, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 1024, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 58162),
('Hm, greetings young one. You are quite a fascinating creature. We don\'t get many of your kind out here. \n\nOr, many of any kind!', '', 277499, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 1024, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 58162),
('I got more questions than answers. What are they looking for down there?\n\nAnd Gallywix... Why did it have to be Gallywix?', '', 277408, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 1024, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 58162),
('', 'Welcome aboard, $c!\n\nThe Princess\'s Pride is nearly ready to head back to the Siren Isle! You ready to go?', 276992, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 1024, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 58162),
('<The machine rumbles atop a pile of steaming rubble as the engine churns  below. The clanging of hammers on metal can be heard ringing from within. After a moment, a voice shouts out to you.>\n\nAye? Need a ride to the Siren Isle?\n\nWell come on then, hop in!', '', 276990, 0, 0, 0, 1, 0, 1024, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 58162),
('<The machine rumbles atop a pile of steaming rubble as the engine churns below. The clanging of hammers on metal can be heard ringing from within. After a moment, a voice shouts out to you.>\n\nNeed a lift to Gundargaz? Hop in!', '', 276979, 0, 0, 0, 1, 0, 1024, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 58162),
('', 'Sure feels good to be back flyin\' on the open breeze after a few years!\n\nSay, you thinkin\' about headin\' back to Dornogal?', 276953, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 1024, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 58162),
('', 'Glad that\'s over. I forgot how much I enjoy a sunny day!', 276793, 0, 0, 5, 0, 0, 1024, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 58162),
('', 'I\'m ready to leave whenever you are!', 276791, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 1024, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 58162),
('Ok, now it\'s your turn. Go hide. One, two, three... better hurry.', 'Ok, now it\'s your turn. Go hide. One, two, three... better hurry.', 276625, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 1024, 69350400, 69350656, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 58162),
('See ya.', 'See ya.', 276624, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 1024, 69347328, 69347584, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 58162),
('Time\'s a wastin\'.', 'Time\'s a wastin\'.', 276623, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 1024, 69346816, 69347072, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 58162),
('We\'ll get it done.', 'We\'ll get it done.', 276622, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 1024, 69346304, 69346560, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 58162),
('Don\'t work too hard.', 'Don\'t work too hard.', 276621, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 1024, 69345792, 69346048, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 58162),
('Quittin\' time!', 'Quittin\' time!', 276620, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 1024, 69345280, 69345536, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 58162),
('I\'m on it!', 'I\'m on it!', 276619, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 1024, 69349888, 69350144, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 58162),
('I hear ya.', 'I hear ya.', 276618, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 1024, 69349376, 69349632, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 58162),
('Yeah?', 'Yeah?', 276617, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 1024, 69348864, 69349120, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 58162),
('What\'s the news?', 'What\'s the news?', 276616, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 1024, 69348352, 69348608, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 58162),
('', 'There is much to learn if we simply listen and observe.', 276615, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 1024, 0, 0, 256, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 58162),
('How ya doin, pal?', 'How ya doin, pal?', 276614, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 1024, 69347840, 69348096, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 58162),
('', 'Ooo, riddles. Which one should we start wiff?', 276444, 0, 0, 1, 0, 0, 1024, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 58162),
('', 'Ooo! An almanac? Farmers use these all da time. How cool!', 276428, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 1024, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 58162),
('', 'Hmm. I bet this \'J\' on here is for a person\'s name.', 276427, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 1024, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 58162),
('', 'Is this for one of those elixirs tat can randomly turn you into a skeleton? Why do people drink tat? So spooky!', 276426, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 1024, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 58162),
('', 'This is quality gnomish engineering. It reminds me of da mechanical chickens. Isn\'t there a mechanical chicken guy?', 276425, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 1024, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 58162),
('', 'Oh! There\'s something inside! I fink tat\'s Orc hair. How interesting!', 276424, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 1024, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 58162),
('', 'Missing items? Which one do you need halp wiff?', 276423, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 1024, 0, 0, 1024, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 58162),
('Parties always have the best food!', '', 276150, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 1024, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 58162),
('', 'Don\'t forget to show off your best mounts while you party!', 276149, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 1024, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 58162),
('', 'You\'re looking quite stylish!', 276124, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 1024, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 58162),
('I hear there is a hearty stew available. A perfect party meal!', '', 276123, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 1024, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 58162),
('Ah, what a way to celebrate the ending of another adventure.', '', 276122, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 1024, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 58162),
('I hear you have had many adventures lately. Perhaps you will soon tell your own stories.', '', 276121, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 1024, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 58162),
('', 'Were you surprised?', 276120, 0, 0, 1, 0, 0, 1024, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 58162),
('I can\'t remember the last time I had a vacation.', '', 276048, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 1024, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 58162),
('We decided to put on a little surprise for you and Alyx for all your hard work.\n\nTake a look around, grab some snacks, and enjoy a deserved rest from your detective work.', '', 276047, 0, 0, 1, 0, 0, 1024, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 58162),
('Hah! I bet you didn\'t see this coming!', '', 276045, 0, 0, 1, 0, 0, 1024, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 58162),
('Ah yes, I\'ve got the order.\n\nI\'m supposed to tell you to go to the northern part of the beach now.', '', 276044, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 1024, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 58162),
('', '<Maru giggles.>\n\nI fink you should go to Wavestrider Beach!', 276042, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 1024, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 58162),
('', 'I fink Detective Jones wants to talk to you again.', 276041, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 1024, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 58162),
('', 'A lucky feast? Didn\'t you meet someone at da beach who had you help wiff somefing like tat?', 276040, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 1024, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 58162),
('Now I just need you to check up on something for me.\n\nI made a request for a \"lucky feast\" that I heard rumors about.\n\nCan you make sure the order has been fulfilled?', '', 276039, 0, 0, 1, 0, 0, 1024, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 58162),
('Ah, perfect.\n\nNow I need you to distribute these letters. They will explain to everyone what has happened.\n\nDon\'t read any of them! The timeline depends on it!', '', 276036, 0, 0, 1, 0, 0, 1024, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 58162),
('', 'You need to hand out da letters to visitors in the area!', 276034, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 1024, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 58162),
('', 'You found all da imposters!\n\nDetective Jones would know what to do next.', 276033, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 1024, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 58162),
('', 'I fink Detective Jones wants you to look around this area and find people tat stand out.\n\nIf you see da same person in more than one place, one of them is probably an imposter!', 276028, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 1024, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 58162),
('Ah! My heart returns to me! \n\nI keep a lock of my dear Olgra\'s hair in this locket. It is irreplaceable. \n\nThank you for delivering this to me.', '', 275549, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 1024, 0, 0, 23296, 60674, 4355, 1, 0, 0, 58162),
('Humph. Why, exactly, are you wasting my time? Leave me be.', '', 275548, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 1024, 0, 0, 4608, 1537, 0, 0, 0, 0, 58162),
('I have lost something precious, indeed.', '', 275547, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 1024, 0, 0, 4352, 1, 0, 0, 0, 0, 58162),
('Whiskers McWhiskerFace! You have returned home!\n\nOh, I thought my dear pet lost for good. Thank you for delivering it to me.\n\nAnd no ransom either? This IS my lucky day!', '', 275542, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 1024, 0, 0, 1024, 4608, 256, 0, 0, 0, 58162),
('Alas, I\'m sorry to say this does not belong to me. I must be going now, but good luck with the ransoming!', '', 275536, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 1024, 0, 0, 4608, 60673, 259, 0, 0, 0, 58162),
('I have, why? Are you here to ransom it? You cad!', '', 275535, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 1024, 0, 0, 4352, 1537, 1280, 0, 0, 0, 58162),
('<Marin grabs the bottle and turns it over in his hands, checking it for any damage.>\n\nBless my coin purse! Do you have any idea how expensive it is to get these engraved like this?\n\nThanks so much for delivering it to me.', '', 275531, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 1024, 0, 0, 45056, 1025, 512, 0, 0, 0, 58162),
('No, I\'m afraid you are mistaken. This clearly belongs to someone else. \n\nNow, if you\'ll excuse me.', '', 275527, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 1024, 0, 0, 60672, 3, 0, 0, 0, 0, 58162),
('I have, yes. I\'m sure it\'s lost to the ages at this point, though.', '', 275523, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 1024, 0, 0, 4352, 1537, 0, 0, 0, 0, 58162),
('<Keeshan lets loose a short gasp as he takes the jade amulet from you.>\n\nI would have been gutted if this was lost forever, but I never doubted the good natures of those gathered here.\n\nThank you for delivering this to me. A thousand times, thank you.', '', 275497, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 1024, 0, 0, 52736, 60673, 16899, 0, 0, 0, 58162),
('<Keeshan looks at the item then slowly back to you.>\n\nDo not bother me with this nonsense.', '', 275492, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 1024, 0, 0, 19712, 258, 0, 0, 0, 0, 58162),
('Maybe. Maybe not. \n\nWhy do you ask?', '', 275491, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 1024, 0, 0, 256, 1536, 0, 0, 0, 0, 58162),
('', 'Why don\'t you try looking around Gadgyzan? I bet you\'ll find a suuuper mysterious traveller!', 275474, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 1024, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 58162),
('Yes, I am the mysterious merchant. I have super ancient relics for you for completing the ancient riddles.\n\nTake them back to your friend!', '', 275471, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 1024, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 58162),
('Oh! Hello traveller!', '', 275468, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 1024, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 58162),
('<Farmer Yoon\'s eyes light up as he takes the journal from you.>\n\nMy grandfather\'s journal! I\'m so happy it was found and turned in. I would have been crushed if this was lost for good. \n\nThank you so much for delivering this to me!', '', 275451, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 1024, 0, 0, 4352, 30209, 16897, 0, 0, 0, 58162),
('I\'m sorry, my what? That isn\'t what I lost. Thanks for getting my hopes up.\n\nIf you\'ll excuse me, I have a celebration to get back to.', '', 275450, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 1024, 0, 0, 4608, 60673, 3, 0, 0, 0, 58162),
('As a matter of fact, I did, yes. Why do you ask?', '', 275419, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 1024, 0, 0, 4352, 1537, 0, 0, 0, 0, 58162),
('', 'Tat sounds like Zul\'Farrak to me!\n\nBut you probably want to stay outside the gates and look around wiff da stick of revealing.', 275366, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 1024, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 58162),
('', 'You found a note? Oh yeah! You have to look for...\n\nI mean, it sounds like there might be somefing in da ruins tat you need to find.\n\nIf it happens to be somefing wiff numbers, you probably have to use them for your finking cap and start at the chest tat\'s there. Just a hunch.\n\n<Maru tries to hide a smile.>', 275348, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 1024, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 58162),
('', '<Maru giggles.>\n\nOohh you need help with the riddle? Look in the south area near da Valley of the Watchers.', 275339, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 1024, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 58162),
('', 'Goodbye, Hannan.', 275216, 0, 0, 0, 102, 0, 1024, 0, 69473280, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 58162),
('May the ancient roots of our people ever thrive beneath your steps.', '', 275215, 0, 0, 0, 70, 0, 1024, 69475584, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 58162),
('I do not understand your conviction, Orweyna.', '', 275214, 0, 0, 0, 70, 0, 1024, 69475840, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 58162),
('Then you will walk it alone.', '', 275212, 0, 0, 0, 70, 0, 1024, 69475328, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 58162),
('', 'Tell the elders that the fault is mine, and mine alone. I will face them in time...but for now,', 275210, 0, 0, 0, 70, 0, 1024, 0, 69474304, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 58162),
('', '<Takes a deep breath.>', 275209, 0, 0, 0, 70, 0, 1024, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 58162),
('The others and I are returning to the cradle to seek forgiveness.', '', 275204, 0, 0, 0, 70, 0, 1024, 69474560, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 58162),
('', 'We cannot give up now.', 275203, 0, 0, 0, 70, 0, 1024, 0, 69472512, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 58162),
('', 'You\'ve seen the growing threats here, Hannan.', 275201, 0, 0, 0, 70, 0, 1024, 0, 69473024, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 58162),
('', 'It is those very traditions that have put our home at risk!', 275199, 0, 0, 0, 70, 0, 1024, 0, 69473536, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 58162),
('We followed you and your visions this far,', '', 275198, 0, 0, 0, 70, 0, 1024, 69474816, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 58162),
('', 'Our goddess is crying out for aid,', 275197, 0, 0, 0, 70, 0, 1024, 0, 69473792, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 58162),
('You\'ve put us all in grave peril.', '', 275196, 0, 0, 0, 70, 0, 1024, 69475072, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 58162),
('This was a mistake, Orweyna.', '', 275195, 0, 0, 0, 70, 0, 1024, 69476096, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 58162),
('', 'Hannan?', 275194, 0, 0, 0, 70, 0, 1024, 0, 69474048, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 58162),
('Cyrce\'s Circlet? Lost?\n\n<Bargus wiggles his wiry mustache as his eyes furrow with thought.>\n\nThat is troublesome. But do not engage your worry yet, $n.\n\nI can use my scanner and... \n\nWorry terminated! It was right here all along!', '', 275112, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 1024, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 58162),
('That\'s our Didi! No off position on the genius switch!', '', 274567, 0, 0, 0, 100, 0, 1024, 68840704, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 58162),
('', 'Oh, believe you me, I know what to do with it. Heh heh heh heh.', 274566, 0, 0, 0, 100, 0, 1024, 0, 68840448, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 58162),
('Soon, you\'ll have more power than you know what to do with.', '', 274564, 0, 0, 0, 100, 0, 1024, 68840192, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 58162),
('', 'I ain\'t in it for the money. I\'m in it for the power.', 274563, 0, 0, 0, 100, 0, 1024, 0, 68839936, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 58162),
('Okay, okay, I get ya. After all, whatcha got cookin\' could be really valuable.', '', 274562, 0, 0, 0, 100, 0, 1024, 68839680, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 58162),
('', 'Hey, I ain\'t lookin\' to blow stuff up. I want a power source... a bunch of batteries!', 274561, 0, 0, 0, 100, 0, 1024, 0, 68839424, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 58162),
('Didya know what was here before us, Didi? An Azerite mine! Some Kul Tiran outfit...', '', 274560, 0, 0, 0, 100, 0, 1024, 68839168, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 58162),
('You know what you should do? Make some explosives! Big bada booms!', '', 274559, 0, 0, 0, 100, 0, 1024, 68838912, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 58162),
('', 'Spoken like a true earthen. A creator should follow her heart. We\'ll find more of those smaller crystals for you.', 274558, 0, 0, 0, 100, 0, 1024, 0, 68838656, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 58162),
('', 'Now I have the inspiration for more intricate creations: lattices, orreries, matrices...', 274557, 0, 0, 0, 100, 0, 1024, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 58162),
('', 'I heard they were mining Azerite. I\'m glad we have more reasonable designs.', 274556, 0, 0, 0, 100, 0, 1024, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 58162),
('', 'More mysteries. Their culture practically vanished overnight. It\'s one of the Crystal\'s biggest enigmas.', 274555, 0, 0, 0, 100, 0, 1024, 0, 68837888, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 58162),
('', 'Really? I haven\'t left the workshop. What have you found? Journals? Letters? Schematics?', 274554, 0, 0, 0, 100, 0, 1024, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 58162),
('', 'It\'s a shame the Kul Tirans didn\'t hear the same song. We found the remains of their mining camp. Their culture didn\'t endure here.', 274552, 0, 0, 0, 100, 0, 1024, 0, 68837376, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 58162),
('', 'That\'s the difference between you and me. You build. I protect. And mark my words: we will need that protection.', 274551, 0, 0, 0, 100, 0, 1024, 0, 68836864, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 58162),
('You need to trust the earthen and the goblins. They\'re not our enemies. We need to work together.', '', 274550, 0, 0, 0, 100, 0, 1024, 68836608, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 58162),
('', 'We\'re not going to war. It\'s coming to us. When the others seize that Crystal, we\'ll need more guards.', 274548, 0, 0, 0, 100, 0, 1024, 0, 68836352, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 58162),
('I don\'t want to go to war again. I want to go home. We\'re closer to our homelands than ever before.', '', 274545, 0, 0, 0, 100, 0, 1024, 68837120, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 58162),
('I didn\'t hear a call to battle. I heard a hymn of healing.', '', 274543, 0, 0, 0, 100, 0, 1024, 68836096, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 58162),
('', 'Excellent. That\'s the kind of support we\'ll need to bolster our troops. We could strengthen our defenses.', 274542, 0, 0, 0, 100, 0, 1024, 0, 68835840, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 58162),
('<Gazix gives you a long look.>\n\nYa know, that\'s ok; I don\'t need you to forgive me. Frankly I can\'t say I blame you... much. \n\nBut all the same, I\'m sorry for all that\'s been done to make ya feel that way.\n\nI hope the small things I do here can be a little start towards a better tomorrow... for all of us. At the end of the day, that\'s all any of us can do really.\n\n<Gazix shrugs with a small smile and resumes picking up trash.>', '', 274300, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 1024, 0, 0, 256, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 58162),
('Quick $n into the cave! Some of these cursed have reached the Singing Tablet!', '', 274278, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 1024, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 58162),
('Task complete. I can hear it singing. It\'s ready for the artifact.', '', 274207, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 1024, 68805120, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 58162),
('', 'The crystal you found is cracked. Let\'s restore it in the forge.', 274204, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 1024, 0, 68804864, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 58162),
('We earthen are no strangers to reading energy signatures from crystalline compounds. But the energy here is... different. \n\nWe\'ve never encountered something like this before.', '', 274142, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 1024, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 58162),
('As much as my curiosity protocol has been activated, the defenses in this structure are relentless. \n\nWe would be wise to regroup at the camp and reassess what we\'ve found. We will return to study more of this crystal at another time.', '', 273996, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 1024, 0, 0, 60672, 3, 0, 0, 0, 0, 58162),
('', 'It has been many years since I have captained a vessel through open skies and over endless waters.\n\nWhen Faerin and General Steelstrike began organizing this expedition to study Lorandel, I volunteered to serve as captain.\n\nI trusted my crew and the Dauntless with my life for over a decade, and I would do so again for another ten more. \n\nBut the Starchaser is a fine ship, and the Dauntless will wait for me.\n\nBeing the first airship to explore the world since our arrival in Hallowfall is quite the claim to fame.', 273995, 0, 0, 5, 0, 0, 1024, 0, 0, 6400, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 58162),
('The energy from these crystals are... extraordinary! For some reason, my device cannot tap into them though.', '', 273990, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 1024, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 58162),
('Heya, pal! Ready to embark on a thrilling adventure?', '', 273989, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 1024, 0, 0, 60672, 3, 0, 0, 0, 0, 58162),
('', 'Woah... What\'s this place?', 273894, 0, 0, 1, 0, 0, 1024, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 58162),
('Hey there, champ!\n\nDidja bring me somethin\'?', 'Hey there, champ!\n\nDidja bring me somethin\'?', 273891, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 1024, 0, 0, 256, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 58162),
('', 'Big singing crystal? Where? Not hear any singing...\n\nMaybe too much wax in ears?', 273758, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 1024, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 58162),
('The signal\'s coming from that cave. It\'s seems like we\'re not the only ones to take interest in it. We need to get in there.', '', 273443, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 1024, 68795904, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 58162),
('And that part... goes over there...', '', 273420, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 1024, 68794368, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 58162),
('Hey, welcome aboard! The earthen and the Arathi are on the island already. We gotta catch up!', '', 273289, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 1024, 68668928, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 58162),
('', 'Imagine: a giant crystal that sings! We\'re investigating on Siren Isle. Care to join us?', 273288, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 1024, 0, 68676608, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 58162),
('Your mind is as dull as your armaments. The latter I could fix it for you... But I won\'t.', '', 273232, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 1024, 68748288, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 58162),
('Fortify your armor. Fortify your will.', '', 273231, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 1024, 68756736, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 58162),
('Forge your own path.', '', 273230, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 1024, 68757504, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 58162),
('Conversation terminated.', '', 273229, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 1024, 68757760, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 58162),
('May you work serve others.', '', 273228, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 1024, 68758016, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 58162),
('How can my hammer serve?', '', 273227, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 1024, 68750592, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 58162),
('Are you here to help the Awakened?', '', 273226, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 1024, 68751360, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 58162),
('My programming has expanded to exploration... and conversation.', '', 273225, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 1024, 68752128, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 58162),
('Conversation initiated.', '', 273224, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 1024, 68752896, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 58162),
('', 'I\'ll do whatever I can for the Kirin Tor.', 273218, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 512, 0, 68674560, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 58162),
('', 'I\'ve studied too hard and too long to give up.', 273217, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 512, 0, 68675840, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 58162),
('', 'Greetings.', 273216, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 512, 0, 68667392, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 58162),
('', 'Be careful.', 273215, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 512, 0, 68660992, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 58162),
('', 'We will see what the future holds for the Kirin Tor.', 273214, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 512, 0, 68695552, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 58162),
('', 'For Dalaran.', 273213, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 512, 0, 68666624, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 58162),
('', 'One upside to the the destruction of Dalaran is that no one has record of me failing my physical education class twice.', 273212, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 512, 0, 68683520, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 58162),
('', 'You\'re why people like animals better.', 273211, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 512, 0, 68697600, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 58162),
('', 'Let me know if I can help.', 273208, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 512, 0, 68678400, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 58162),
('', 'Till the next time we meet.', 273207, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 512, 0, 68691968, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 58162),
('', 'For Dalaran.', 273206, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 512, 0, 68666368, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 58162);

INSERT INTO `broadcast_text` (`Text`, `Text1`, `ID`, `LanguageID`, `ConditionID`, `EmotesID`, `Flags`, `ChatBubbleDurationMs`, `VoiceOverPriorityID`, `SoundKitID1`, `SoundKitID2`, `EmoteID1`, `EmoteID2`, `EmoteID3`, `EmoteDelay1`, `EmoteDelay2`, `EmoteDelay3`, `VerifiedBuild`) VALUES
('', 'Peace be with you.', 273205, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 512, 0, 68684288, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 58162),
('', 'The Kirin Tor need my aid.', 273204, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 512, 0, 68689408, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 58162),
('', 'I am here to help.', 273202, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 512, 0, 68669952, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 58162),
('', 'Fascinating. We\'ve only just begun our exploration. It\'s time to answer the call to adventure.', 273161, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 1024, 0, 68799488, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 58162),
('', 'Now you can discover more mysteries hidden on the island. Seek and you will find.', 273159, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 1024, 0, 68799232, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 58162),
('', 'Can you feel it, $p? The artifact has awakened!', 273155, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 1024, 0, 68798976, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 58162),
('', 'The crystal is calling to the ring...', 273153, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 1024, 0, 68798464, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 58162),
('This is... more of an adventure than even I desired. We should get this artifact back to the workshop for examination.', '', 273145, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 1024, 68798208, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 58162),
('By the titans! An ancient construct?', '', 273144, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 1024, 68797696, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 58162),
('This bears closer examination. After you. See what you can find...', '', 273142, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 1024, 68797952, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 58162),
('What\'s this? An ancient shrine... another crystal facet... and the gleam of something promising...', '', 273140, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 1024, 68797440, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 58162),
('The signal is getting stronger... it\'s coming from that chamber...', '', 273139, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 1024, 68796672, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 58162),
('Echoes of the past! This structure clearly has a history...', '', 273138, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 1024, 68796928, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 58162),
('Remarkable! The signal\'s energy surrounds this structure. How deep does this go?', '', 273137, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 1024, 68796416, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 58162),
('Analyzing. This tablet\'s markings seem... familiar.', '', 273135, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 1024, 68797184, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 58162),
('Fascinating. The energy is focused through that tablet...', '', 273133, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 1024, 68795648, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 58162),
('Intriguing. I\'m detecting a secondary reading from the north. This requires more Investigation.', '', 273132, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 1024, 68796160, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 58162),
('That\'s it! Its energies are beyond my capacity to process. The crystal extends far beneath the surface!', '', 273131, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 1024, 68795392, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 58162),
('Signal augmented. One more reading should calibrate the device.', '', 273130, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 1024, 68794880, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 58162),
('This singing crystal is remarkably like Beledar. We should treat it with reverence.', '', 273129, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 1024, 68794624, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 58162),
('I\'ll set some metal pylons to focus the signal. Meet me over the hill.', '', 273128, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 1024, 68795136, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 58162),
('Task complete. Now we can use the crystal\'s signature to track its facets.', '', 273127, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 1024, 68794112, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 58162),
('', 'Whaddya need? Batteries? These puppies should keep the scanner juiced up. You\'re good to go!', 273123, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 1024, 0, 68793344, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 58162),
('Hmmm. My sacred crystals could help harmonize your readings, but you\'ll need more power...', '', 273121, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 1024, 68793600, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 58162),
('', 'Interpreting a massive crystal\'s energy is a specialized process. Maybe the Arathi learned something from Beledar...', 273106, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 1024, 0, 68793088, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 58162),
('We earthen are here to study the crystal. The goblins and the Arathi... we are still processing how to collaborate.', '', 273105, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 1024, 68793856, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 58162),
('Are you here to lend a hand? Admirable. Perhaps we can all work together.', '', 273104, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 1024, 68792832, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 58162),
('The competition\'s hard at work. You should say hello to the neighbors. Real friendly-like.', '', 273103, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 1024, 68792576, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 58162),
('See? We\'re late to the party. Meet me below. And watch your step! Heh heh heh.', '', 273102, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 1024, 68792320, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 58162),
('Thank you, Jaina. And good luck.', '', 272871, 0, 0, 0, 4, 0, 1024, 68651520, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 58162),
('', 'Meryl can assist me. Aethas should have a key role as well. I will go back and speak to them.', 272870, 0, 0, 0, 4, 0, 1024, 0, 68650752, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 58162),
('I need rest, Jaina. But... I promise I won\'t stay away for long.', '', 272869, 0, 0, 0, 4, 0, 2560, 68648960, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 58162),
('', 'Khadgar...', 272868, 0, 0, 0, 4, 0, 2560, 0, 68650240, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 58162),
('And that is why it should be you who starts putting the pieces back together.', '', 272867, 0, 0, 0, 4, 0, 2560, 68648192, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 58162),
('', 'Study and passing on my knowledge appeals to me. But I have to think about the ramifications of such a drastic change.', 272842, 0, 0, 0, 4, 0, 2560, 0, 68651264, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 58162),
('Safety is a benefit, yes.', '', 272836, 0, 0, 0, 4, 0, 2560, 68649216, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 58162),
('', 'It would keep us mobile and decentralized. A tragedy like Dalaran would not happen again.', 272835, 0, 0, 0, 4, 0, 2560, 0, 68649984, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 58162),
('We can still fulfill that mission by investigating. Training. Advising.', '', 272832, 0, 0, 0, 4, 0, 2560, 68652288, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 58162),
('', 'But we have a duty to protect the Alliance--and Azeroth.', 272831, 0, 0, 0, 4, 0, 2560, 0, 68648704, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 58162),
('', 'Like starting over? Returning to study and research?', 272830, 0, 0, 0, 4, 0, 2560, 0, 68650496, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 58162),
('No, the mages who have answered the call... We have an opportunity. No council. No rank.', '', 272824, 0, 0, 0, 4, 0, 2560, 68651008, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 58162),
('', 'Then... our new Kirin Tor is over before it began.', 272823, 0, 0, 0, 4, 0, 2560, 0, 68652032, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 58162),
('I\'m afraid the news from outside is bleak. We lost all but a few after amassing at Dalaran.', '', 272820, 0, 0, 0, 4, 0, 2560, 68649728, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 58162),
('', 'I was. But we should speak about the future of the Kirin Tor sooner rather than later.', 272814, 0, 0, 0, 68, 0, 2560, 0, 68649472, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 58162),
('Jaina, I thought you were staying to help in the Tranquil Strand.', '', 272809, 0, 0, 0, 68, 0, 2560, 68677120, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 58162),
('Kalecgos, I... thank you.', '', 272800, 0, 0, 0, 68, 0, 2560, 68653824, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 58162),
('For now, you need rest. Let me put the burden on my wings for awhile.', '', 272799, 0, 0, 0, 68, 0, 2560, 68653312, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 58162),
('They will come.', '', 272798, 0, 0, 0, 68, 0, 2560, 68654592, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 58162),
('I have spent most my adult years among the Sacredites studying the properties of the radiant remnants--small, crystalline fragments found in Hallowfall.\n\nBeyond the walls of the Priory, I had seen or experienced very little.\n\nI was nervous to embark on the Starchaser from the Isle of Dorn, but I... I am glad I did.\n\nFor the first time in ages, I feel inspired and enlightened.\n\nMaybe it\'s the rhythm of Lorandel\'s song, or maybe it\'s just the salty air...', 'I have spent most my adult years among the Sacredites studying the properties of the radiant remnants--small, crystalline fragments found in Hallowfall.\n\nBeyond the walls of the Priory, I had seen or experienced very little.\n\nI was nervous to embark on the Starchaser from the Isle of Dorn, but I... I am glad I did.\n\nFor the first time in ages, I feel inspired and enlightened.\n\nMaybe it\'s the rhythm of Lorandel\'s song, or maybe it\'s just the salty air...', 272794, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 1024, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 58162),
('And yet, here I am. Still alone. The Kirin Tor...', '', 272749, 0, 0, 0, 68, 0, 2560, 68648448, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 58162),
('To continue to fight and then rebuild... that\'s more than anyone would ask of you.', '', 272748, 0, 0, 0, 68, 0, 2560, 68654848, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 58162),
('You\'re a survivor--a victim of this tragedy.', '', 272747, 0, 0, 0, 68, 0, 2560, 68655616, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 58162),
('Aethas, none of it was your fault.', '', 272746, 0, 0, 0, 68, 0, 2560, 68652800, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 58162),
('I know very little about what has transpired here. But...', '', 272745, 0, 0, 0, 68, 0, 2560, 68653568, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 58162),
('What horror comes here and takes more of us away?', '', 272744, 0, 0, 0, 68, 0, 2560, 68655104, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 58162),
('Of letting everyone we have lost down again. If I slip. If... if I sleep. What then?', '', 272743, 0, 0, 0, 68, 0, 2560, 68654080, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 58162),
('Then of what?', '', 272742, 0, 0, 0, 68, 0, 2560, 68654336, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 58162),
('Fear isn\'t part of it. Or... not fear of nerubians or... or even Xal\'atath.', '', 272741, 0, 0, 0, 68, 0, 2560, 68653056, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 58162),
('What you have told me makes me afraid for you, Aethas.', '', 272740, 0, 0, 0, 68, 0, 2560, 68655360, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 58162),
('', 'I\'m about to break my wand over your head if you don\'t quit that.', 272735, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 512, 0, 68675328, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 58162),
('', 'We can do this. We are Kirin Tor.', 272734, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 512, 0, 68693248, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 58162),
('', 'Be safe, now.', 272733, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 512, 0, 68661248, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 58162),
('', 'For Dalaran!', 272732, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 512, 0, 68665600, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 58162),
('', 'What you need?', 272731, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 512, 0, 68696320, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 58162),
('', 'I heed the call of the Kirin Tor.', 272730, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 512, 0, 68671744, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 58162),
('', 'Salutations, my friend.', 272729, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 512, 0, 68685824, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 58162),
('Hands off my Kirin Tor tabard. It\'s a rare collectors item now. Probably.', '', 272728, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 512, 68687104, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 58162),
('Farewell.', '', 272727, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 512, 68665088, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 58162),
('Return if you need my aid.', '', 272726, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 512, 68685568, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 58162),
('For Dalaran.', '', 272725, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 512, 68666112, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 58162),
('When the Kirin Tor calls, I answer.', '', 272724, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 512, 68696576, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 58162),
('I stand with the Kirin Tor.', '', 272723, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 512, 68673280, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 58162),
('Greetings.', '', 272722, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 512, 68667648, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 58162),
('', 'Hey! Haven\'t I been through enough? Sheesh, some people.', 272719, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 512, 0, 68668672, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 58162),
('', 'Oh, what a mess...', 272718, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 512, 0, 68696064, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 58162),
('', 'For Dalaran.', 272717, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 512, 0, 68665856, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 58162),
('', 'Be seeing ya!', 272716, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 512, 0, 68661504, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 58162),
('', 'Need a hand?', 272715, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 512, 0, 68681216, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 58162),
('', 'The Kirin Tor needed me, so... Here I am!', 272714, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 512, 0, 68689664, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 58162),
('', 'Hey there.', 272713, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 512, 0, 68668416, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 58162),
('Are you volunteering as a test subject? I didn\'t think so.', '', 272712, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 1024, 68698368, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 58162),
('Begone.', '', 272711, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 1024, 68699648, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 58162),
('You would not understand my experiments anyway.', '', 272710, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 1024, 68699392, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 58162),
('Where was I...', '', 272709, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 1024, 68698880, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 58162),
('Take your leave then.', '', 272708, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 1024, 68700160, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 58162),
('Another interruption?', '', 272707, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 1024, 68698112, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 58162),
('Can you not see there is work to be done?', '', 272706, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 1024, 68699904, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 58162),
('I do not have time for pleasantries.', '', 272705, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 512, 68698624, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 58162),
('Why are you speaking?', '', 272704, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 512, 68699136, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 58162),
('Shutting... down.', 'Shutting... down.', 272691, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 1024, 68748544, 68748800, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 58162),
('Battle begins!', 'Battle begins!', 272690, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 1024, 68758272, 68758528, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 58162),
('No more patience.', 'No more patience.', 272689, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 1024, 68758784, 68759040, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 58162),
('Experience combat!', 'Experience combat!', 272688, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 1024, 68759296, 68759552, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 58162),
('Intervention required!', 'Intervention required!', 272687, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 1024, 68759808, 68760064, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 58162),
('I will carry many memorable experiences back to the Archive, but for obvious reasons, you will not be one of them.', 'I will carry many memorable experiences back to the Archives, but for obvious reasons, you will not be one of them.', 272686, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 1024, 68631808, 68632064, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 58162),
('Jastor Gallywix is back in business!', '', 272645, 0, 0, 0, 102, 0, 1024, 68595968, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 58162),
('Big things are coming, and if you want to be part of it, you better fall in line.', '', 272644, 0, 0, 0, 102, 0, 1024, 68595712, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 58162),
('Look, pal! The only opportunity here is the one I gave you.', '', 272643, 0, 0, 0, 102, 0, 1024, 68595456, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 58162),
('Are you what passes for an adventurer these days? I should have stayed retired.', '', 272575, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 512, 68659712, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 58162),
('We will prevail. We always do.', '', 272574, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 512, 68695296, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 58162),
('Dark times always end. Remember that.', '', 272573, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 512, 68663040, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 58162),
('Power corrupts. Magic even more so. Guard yourself.', '', 272572, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 512, 68685056, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 58162),
('I am here to help. Not to lead.', '', 272571, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 512, 68670208, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 58162),
('Dalaran\'s loss pains me as well.', '', 272570, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 512, 68669184, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 58162),
('I feel my... experience is relevant here.', '', 272569, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 512, 68676352, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 58162),
('Transaction complete.', 'Transaction complete.', 272560, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 1024, 68746752, 68747008, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 58162),
('Every sale tells a story.', 'Every sale tells a story.', 272559, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 1024, 68747264, 68747520, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 58162),
('Find me something memorable.', 'Find me something memorable.', 272558, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 1024, 68747776, 68748032, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 58162),
('Show me what you\'ve found.', 'Show me what you\'ve found.', 272557, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 1024, 68745216, 68745472, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 58162),
('Something new to trade?', 'Something new to trade?', 272556, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 1024, 68745728, 68745984, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 58162),
('Treasures from far and wide.', 'Treasures from far and wide.', 272555, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 1024, 68746240, 68746496, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 58162),
('Only you know your path.', 'Only you know your path.', 272554, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 1024, 68753664, 68753920, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 58162),
('Another experience awaits.', 'Another experience awaits.', 272553, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 1024, 68754176, 68754432, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 58162),
('We have much to learn.', 'We have much to learn.', 272552, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 1024, 68754688, 68754944, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 58162),
('May your journey be safe.', 'May your journey be safe.', 272551, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 1024, 68755200, 68755456, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 58162),
('Come back with new stories.', 'Come back with new stories.', 272550, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 1024, 68755712, 68755968, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 58162),
('Adventure continues.', 'Adventure continues.', 272549, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 1024, 68756224, 68756480, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 58162),
('Journey onward.', 'Journey onward.', 272548, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 1024, 68756992, 68757248, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 58162),
('Your path led to me.', 'Your path led to me.', 272547, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 1024, 68749056, 68749312, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 58162),
('Stories requested.', 'Stories requested.', 272546, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 1024, 68749568, 68749824, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 58162),
('What have you experienced?', 'What have you experienced?', 272545, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 1024, 68750080, 68750336, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 58162),
('Tell me of your travels.', 'Tell me of your travels.', 272544, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 1024, 68750848, 68751104, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 58162),
('A chance to converse!', 'A chance to converse!', 272543, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 1024, 68751616, 68751872, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 58162),
('Appreciate the mundane.', 'Appreciate the mundane.', 272542, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 1024, 68752384, 68752640, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 58162),
('Seen anything new?', 'Seen anything new?', 272541, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 1024, 68753152, 68753408, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 58162),
('', 'Precise and methodical--that is the earthen way. The steady ringing of an anvil is like the tempo of a familiar melody. Iterations and inspirations are complex variations of musical motif. \n\nOthers might prefer explosive results, meditative bliss, or rapturous inspiration, but for me, the best work is reliable and tactile work.', 272495, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 1024, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 58162),
('', 'Your thoughts align with mine. If we found more of the smaller crystals, I could make enduring wonderworks.', 272485, 0, 0, 0, 100, 0, 1024, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 58162),
('The life of a shopkeeper is somewhat appealing, actually.', '', 272467, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 512, 68690176, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 58162),
('I\'ll see if I can conjure up more later.', '', 272466, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 512, 68675072, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 58162),
('Thank you for your patronage.', '', 272465, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 512, 68687360, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 58162),
('All these items come from my personal stock.', '', 272464, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 512, 68658688, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 58162),
('I have prepared an assortment of items I hope will help you.', '', 272463, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 512, 68671488, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 58162),
('Only the best prices for my friends.', '', 272462, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 512, 68683776, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 58162),
('', 'Perhaps it was calling to the spark of the Worldsoul within you. We\'ve been searching the island to learn more.', 272430, 0, 0, 0, 100, 0, 1024, 0, 68801280, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 58162),
('', 'This morning, I heard the Siren Crystal sing to me, ringing with an intricate melody.', 272429, 0, 0, 0, 100, 0, 1024, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 58162),
('', 'You seem fascinated with those crystals. I was watching your process earlier. What is it about them that inspires you?', 272428, 0, 0, 0, 100, 0, 1024, 0, 68800768, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 58162),
('', 'I\'m boostin\' their energy! You could make some powerful artifacts with these babies!', 272427, 0, 0, 0, 100, 0, 1024, 0, 68802560, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 58162),
('Yeah yeah yeah, you\'ve got a headache. But, ah, whatcha makin\'? We found you a whole kit and kaboodle of crystals!', '', 272426, 0, 0, 0, 100, 0, 1024, 68802304, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 58162),
('', 'The Siren Crystal... it was making a racket this morning! Like a pot banging in my head! Still, it gave me some ideas...', 272425, 0, 0, 0, 100, 0, 1024, 0, 68802048, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 58162),
('Hey, what\'s the good news?', '', 272424, 0, 0, 0, 100, 0, 1024, 68801792, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 58162),
('Yes! Its music soothed me. Now I\'m crafting more healing crystals. They\'ll bring solace to our Empire.', '', 272415, 0, 0, 0, 100, 0, 1024, 68800512, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 58162),
('', 'That sounds like the kind of inspiration we\'d receive from Beledar.', 272412, 0, 0, 0, 100, 0, 1024, 0, 68800256, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 58162),
('This morning, the Siren Crystal sang a reverent hymn to me... a restorative anthem from a bygone age.', '', 272407, 0, 0, 0, 100, 0, 1024, 68800000, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 58162),
('', 'What are you making? You seem... inspired.', 272404, 0, 0, 0, 100, 0, 1024, 0, 68799744, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 58162),
('My friend, a crime against the arts has been performed this day! Alas, a trickster has hidden many needed items about the area.\n\nPerhaps you can make sense of this list they left behind?', '', 271694, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 1024, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 58162),
('', 'Oooh! I fink you should look for something tat makes music.', 271693, 0, 0, 1, 0, 0, 1024, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 58162),
('', 'Hmm, where would fings echo... Maybe somewhere big backstage?', 271692, 0, 0, 1, 0, 0, 1024, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 58162),
('', 'It sounds like you need to look somewhere in da audience for this one!\n\nMaybe underneath somefing big...', 271691, 0, 0, 1, 0, 0, 1024, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 58162),
('', 'Try looking somewhere behind da stage where da writers work.', 271690, 0, 0, 1, 0, 0, 1024, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 58162),
('<Skeletal remains sit slumped against the rocks. Their ribcage and legs are shattered as if crushed by something heavy.\n\nIn their outstretched hand sits a gleaming, rune-carved ring.>', '', 271433, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 1024, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 58162),
('', 'Admiration expressed. The Vrykul are leaving. Now we can continue researching that crystal and its energies.', 271411, 0, 0, 1, 0, 0, 1024, 0, 68774656, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 58162),
('', 'How curious. Vrykul are searching the island again. Each incursion brings destruction. We require... strategic intervention.', 271410, 0, 0, 1, 0, 0, 1024, 0, 68775424, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 58162),
('', 'Well done! An exemplary display! The cave is open. Troops! Deploy!', 271394, 0, 132784, 0, 0, 0, 1024, 0, 68778752, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 58162),
('', 'Look lively! I want that cave entrance cleared! Run out the guns. Commence bombardment!', 271393, 0, 132784, 0, 0, 0, 1024, 0, 68777472, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 58162),
('', 'The wild energy of that elemental had to be contained. However, studying its remains may reveal the answers to its uncontrolled nature.', 271392, 0, 0, 1, 0, 0, 1024, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 58162),
('That looked pretty disgusting. I\'m glad you handled it instead of me!', '', 271389, 0, 0, 1, 0, 0, 1024, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 58162),
('', 'Reliable as always. The Empire appreciates stalwart allies. Our forces on high remain vigilant.', 271385, 0, 0, 1, 0, 0, 1024, 0, 68778240, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 58162),
('', 'Our troops will strike at this draconic horror within its lair. A barrage of cannon fire will reveal its presence. Prepare yourselves!', 271380, 0, 0, 1, 0, 0, 1024, 0, 68777984, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 58162),
('', 'We will not tolerate a threat to our airship on this island, no matter where it may hide. Allies of the Arathi, prepare for battle!', 271379, 0, 0, 1, 0, 0, 1024, 0, 68778496, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 58162),
('', 'I\'ve dispatched a team of kobolds to excavate the site and examine it firsthand. Assistance requested.', 271372, 0, 0, 1, 0, 0, 1024, 0, 68777216, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 58162),
('', 'Can you sense that power? I can feel it. Elemental fury is building, resonating with the crystal.', 271371, 0, 0, 1, 0, 0, 1024, 0, 68776704, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 58162),
('<The contraption appears inert. All mechanisms are unlocked.>', '', 271367, 0, 128790, 0, 0, 0, 1024, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 58162),
('Whaddya think washed down that drain? Maybe it\'s treasure. Or maybe it\'s monsters. And maybe those monsters have treasure!', '', 271361, 0, 0, 5, 0, 0, 1024, 68779008, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 58162),
('Get your feet moving. We got a tunnel to blast open! This kaboom oughtta be good!', '', 271360, 0, 0, 1, 0, 0, 1024, 68776960, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 58162),
('', 'Keep out of trouble, and make sure Brinthe always knows where ye are.', 271321, 0, 0, 0, 68, 0, 1024, 0, 68034304, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 58162),
('', '<laughs> And knowing you, you\'ll find it all.', 271320, 0, 0, 0, 68, 0, 1024, 0, 68034048, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 58162),
('', 'Are you sure about staying, Dagran? You could return home with us and study there...', 271319, 0, 0, 0, 68, 0, 1024, 0, 68033792, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 58162),
('Don\'t worry about me. All wounds heal... in time.', '', 271313, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 512, 68664320, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 58162),
('We must continue to pursue Xal\'atath. No matter the cost.', '', 271312, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 512, 68694016, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 58162),
('As always, we have much to discuss.', '', 271311, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 512, 68660224, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 58162),
('I am glad to see you still in the thick of things.', '', 271310, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 512, 68669696, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 58162),
('Xal\'atath left destruction in her wake. But we will persevere.', '', 271305, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 512, 68696832, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 58162),
('Nice chatting with you, old friend.', '', 271304, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 512, 68681472, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 58162),
('Be careful out there.', '', 271303, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 512, 68660736, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 58162),
('All that has been lost can be regained.', '', 271302, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 512, 68658432, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 58162),
('Stop it. You\'re giving me grey hairs, and I have too many for my age already!', '', 271301, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 512, 68686848, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 58162),
('The Dragon Isles... Khaz Algar... Just how many more islands have we misplaced that we will find again?', '', 271300, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 1024, 68689152, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 58162),
('Don\'t work too hard.', 'Don\'t work too hard.', 271292, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 1024, 68592384, 68592640, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 58162),
('<The contraption hums with energy. There appears to be $27004w locked |4mechanism:mechanisms;.>', '', 271288, 0, 128790, 0, 0, 0, 1024, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 58162),
('Quittin\' time?', 'Quittin\' time?', 271290, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 1024, 68591872, 68592128, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 58162),
('What\'s the news?', 'What\'s the news?', 271289, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 1024, 68593408, 68593664, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 58162),
('How ya doin, pal?', 'How ya doin, pal?', 271286, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 1024, 68592896, 68593152, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 58162),
('Do not worry. This is not the end of the Kirin Tor.', '', 271284, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 1024, 68663808, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 58162),
('You can count on me for support.', '', 271283, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 1024, 68697344, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 58162),
('Call on me again, and I will follow.', '', 271282, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 1024, 68662272, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 58162),
('May there be fairer skies ahead.', '', 271281, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 1024, 68679936, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 58162),
('Mistakes have been made. But... we can learn from them.', '', 271280, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 1024, 68680448, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 58162),
('We must safeguard what is left of Dalaran.', '', 271279, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 1024, 68694272, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 58162),
('I will do whatever I can for the Kirin Tor.', '', 271278, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 1024, 68673792, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 58162),
('In the darkest of times, we need the truest of friends.', '', 271277, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 1024, 68676864, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 58162),
('<This contraption is non-functional.>', '', 271273, 0, 128790, 0, 0, 0, 1024, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 58162),
('Are you here to talk to Alleria too? I\'ve got word that there\'s a load of goblin activity down in the Ringing Deeps.\n\nI think she\'s got other things on her mind, though.', '', 271250, 0, 0, 1, 0, 0, 1024, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 58162),
('Best of luck to you, Orweyna. One day when you\'ve found what you\'re looking for, I hope you too find your way home.', '', 271249, 0, 0, 2, 68, 0, 1024, 68608512, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 58162),
('', 'You are kind, Magni. I will consider your words carefully.', 271248, 0, 0, 2, 68, 0, 1024, 0, 68608256, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 58162),
('Look for those who will walk the path with you. If I\'ve learned anythin\', it\'s that we\'ll always need each other to not lose ourselves on the journey.', '', 271247, 0, 0, 1, 68, 0, 1024, 68608000, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 58162),
('Aye. It can be lonely, followin\' a path that others can\'t see. But don\'t make the same mistake I did, puttin\' it all on yourself.', '', 271246, 0, 0, 273, 68, 0, 1024, 68607744, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 58162),
('', 'Her voice has led me far from my home, seeking a truth I know she wishes to reveal, but my kin, they... do not understand.', 271245, 0, 0, 1, 68, 0, 1024, 0, 68607488, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 58162),
('Goddess? You mean Azeroth? Aye- I was her speaker for many years, but she\'s let me go from that service.', '', 271244, 0, 0, 6, 68, 0, 1024, 68607232, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 58162),
('', 'I am called Orweyna. I\'ve been told you too have heard the voice of the goddess.', 271243, 0, 0, 2, 68, 0, 1024, 0, 68606976, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 58162),
('Ach, and who\'s this?', '', 271242, 0, 0, 6, 68, 0, 1024, 68606720, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 58162),
('Yes, mum.', '', 271241, 0, 0, 273, 68, 0, 1024, 68606464, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 58162),
('', 'And knowing you, you\'ll find it all. Keep out of trouble, and make sure Brinthe always knows where ye are.', 271240, 0, 0, 1, 68, 0, 1024, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 58162),
('I\'m sure, ma. There\'s still so much knowledge here yet to be discovered!', '', 271239, 0, 0, 1, 68, 0, 1024, 68605952, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 58162),
('', 'Are you sure about staying, Dagran? You could return home with us and study there...', 271238, 0, 0, 6, 68, 0, 1024, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 58162),
('Well, best be setting sail to Ironforge. No sense in dawdling.', '', 271237, 0, 0, 1, 68, 0, 1024, 68605440, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 58162),
('', 'There is so much to discover on this island!', 271121, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 1024, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 58162),
('', 'Well, if it ain\'t my favorite adventurer!\n\nHow ya doin\', hon?', 271120, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 1024, 0, 0, 60672, 3, 0, 0, 0, 0, 58162),
('<Bargus is focused on the work in front of him as golden sparks flare up from each swing of his hammer.>', '', 271117, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 1024, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 58162),
('We shall build our strength not from dominion or deceit, but from dedication to learning and magic.', '', 271084, 0, 0, 0, 4, 0, 1024, 68695040, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 58162),
('Dalaran\'s destruction almost destroyed me. But it is not an end, it is an opportunity--to do things right this time.', '', 271083, 0, 0, 0, 4, 0, 1024, 68662784, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 58162),
('', 'A mana bomb. This is a worst-case scenario. And we only have ourselves to blame.', 271081, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 2048, 0, 68657152, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 58162),
('More mages are arriving to lend their strength. We need to start planning how we want to spend our resources.', '', 271051, 0, 0, 0, 68, 0, 1792, 68680704, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 58162),
('The Dragon Isles can endure a little longer without me. We have much work to do.', '', 271050, 0, 0, 0, 68, 0, 1792, 68688896, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 58162),
('', 'Are you going to stay, Kalecgos?', 271049, 0, 0, 0, 68, 0, 1792, 0, 68659456, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 58162),
('I look forward to our future as the Kirin Tor... and friends.', '', 271047, 0, 0, 0, 4, 0, 1024, 68672512, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 58162),
('Good. Because this old man is tired. I will go to Dornogal to rest. And then start rebuilding the connections we have lost.', '', 271045, 0, 0, 0, 68, 0, 1792, 68667136, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 58162),
('What brings ye here? Have ye come to say goodbye?', '', 270995, 0, 0, 1, 0, 0, 1024, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 58162),
('Me? I\'m on the trail of some big operation in the Ringing Deeps. Why are there so many goblins working right at the edge of the cave? \n\nWhy are there so many different cartels in one place? It\'s not even our annual convention!\n\nAnd who the blast is in charge of it all?\n\nThings like that. Questions, questions.', '', 270994, 0, 0, 1, 0, 0, 1024, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 58162),
('I haven\'t seen this many goblins moving around in one place since... well, it\'s been a while. Kezan comes to mind. \n\nSomething big has to be happening.', '', 270991, 0, 0, 1, 0, 0, 1024, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 58162),
('Yeah, that\'s the one! Anyway, he showed up, threw some rocks around and next thing ya know we all got to join the Horde.\n\n<Gazix pauses thoughtfully.>\n\nHe was taller than I expected.', '', 270979, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 1024, 0, 0, 256, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 58162),
('Oh, yeah. Um... what\'s his name? Big important leader guy. The orc who does the stuff with the elements?', '', 270974, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 1024, 0, 0, 256, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 58162),
('Yeah, unfortunately a buncha us got turned in some ritual... and well, it was them or us.\n\n<Gazix lets out a long sigh.>\n\n Still feel bad about all the folks we lost though.', '', 270973, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 1024, 0, 0, 256, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 58162),
('<Gazix pauses for a moment.>\n\n Because I got to see places on Azeroth that weren\'t fulla garbage and was able to get a fresh start. Got to meet other folks just tryin\' to survive.\n\nAnd... I got to witness a lot of the destruction we goblins have caused firsthand... along with the distaste a lot of races have for us as a result. An\' it\'s not like we don\'t deserve a lot of that hostility either. As a whole we\'ve done some... less than savory things.\n\nBut seein\' all that made me appreciate Gazlowe\'s vision. It made me want more... for all goblins. So even if it\'s just pickin\' up some trash on an island no one\'s ever heard of before, I feel like I\'m helpin\' out.', '', 270972, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 1024, 0, 0, 256, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 58162),
('<Gazix waves his hand dismissively.>\n\nYeah, Gallywix made us all get on a boat. He was going to force us to work in Azshara.\n\nAnyway, when that ship exploded we washed up onto an island, then got chased by zombies, got saved by that important orc guy and then wound up in the streets of Orgrimmar. \n\nIt was an eventful trip to say the least.', '', 270968, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 1024, 0, 0, 256, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 58162),
('It\'s a small island in the South Seas. It\'s where the Bilgewater Cartel is from... and it was filthy. If you think we\'re bad at pickin\' up after ourselves normally you\'d never wanna go there. \n\nI hear Undermine is a pretty similar story.\n\nAnyway, on Kezan there was this slum called Drudgetown... that\'s where I lived.\n\nA handful of years back the island exploded and Gallywix tried to indenture a lot of us, and it was a whole thing.\n\n<Gazix shrugs.>\n\nHonestly, that damn island explodin\' was probably one of the best things that coulda happened to me.', '', 270966, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 1024, 0, 0, 256, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 58162),
('Well that\'s a surprise! Didn\'t think most folks had. That filthy little island is where the Bilgewater Cartel is from. \n\nThere were some slums there called Drudgetown. I ain\'t proud to admit it, but that\'s where I\'m from. Same with Jack over there.\n\n<Gazix motions toward Jack the Hammer.>\n\nAnyway, the island exploded and Gallywix tried to indenture a lot of us, and it was a whole thing.\n\n<Gazix shrugs.>\n\nHonestly, that damn island explodin\' was probably one of the best things that coulda happened to me.', '', 270965, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 1024, 0, 0, 256, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 58162),
('S\'that so? Can\'t imagine why you\'d wanna go back, honestly. Can\'t really imagine why anyone would. You musta had a real compelling reason.\n\nDunno if you ever made it to whatever\'s left of Drudgetown, but that\'s the gutter I lived in back in the day.\n\nThat damn island explodin\' was probably one of the best things that coulda happened to me.', '', 270964, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 1024, 0, 0, 256, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 58162),
('Yeah? Huh, I thought you kinda looked familiar. Glad to see ya made it off the island too pal.\n\nYou remember Drudgetown, right?\n\n<Gazix shudders.>\n\nWell that\'s where I\'m from originally. Ugh, I can still smell it no matter how hard I try to forget.\n\nThat damn island exploding was probably one of the best things that coulda happened to me. \n\nSorry if it put you in a rough spot, but it looks like you\'ve done ok for yourself. I don\'t know that everyone that survived can say the same, but I, for one, am grateful that giant fiery lizard caused that chain reaction or whatever.', '', 270963, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 1024, 0, 0, 256, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 58162),
('<Gazix lets out an annoyed sigh.>\n\nI know! You ain\'t the first person to point that out to me. Why do you think I\'m here doing this?\n\nI hate garbage. I hate we leave so much... stuff behind!', '', 270853, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 1024, 0, 0, 256, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 58162),
('', 'Then we are all in agreement. We will start anew. For the Kirin Tor. For all of us.', 270852, 0, 0, 0, 68, 0, 1024, 0, 68690432, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 58162),
('Let us pledge then that the new Kirin Tor will be different. No more councils, no more floating cities, and no more meddling in world affairs.', '', 270851, 0, 0, 0, 68, 0, 1024, 68678656, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 58162),
('I admit I was blinded by the ivory towers of Dalaran... I believed the Kirin Tor\'s wisdom was nigh infallible.', '', 270850, 0, 0, 0, 68, 0, 1792, 68669440, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 58162),
('', 'Agreed. We must move forward with intention. And learn from the mistakes we were too prideful to before.', 270849, 0, 0, 0, 68, 0, 1792, 0, 68657920, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 58162),
('We rebuild. But not just brick and mortar. We need changes to our foundation--to us.', '', 270848, 0, 0, 0, 68, 0, 1024, 68694528, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 58162),
('So... what now?', '', 270847, 0, 0, 1, 68, 0, 1792, 68686592, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 58162),
('<Gazix gives you a measured look.>\n\nYou ever heard of the island of Kezan?', '', 270844, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 1024, 0, 0, 256, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 58162),
('<Gazix pauses, and a look of surprise flashes across his face. He smiles broadly before he turns back to picking up more garbage.>\n\nI hate trash!\n\n<Gazix sigh.>\n\nI\'m probably the only goblin that\'s ever yelled that, huh? \"Another goblin\'s trash is another goblin\'s treasure...\"\n\nYeah well, some trash is just... trash.', '', 270824, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 1024, 0, 0, 256, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 58162),
('', 'Ney\'leia takes a long look at Orweyna, then shakes her head and sighs.', 270797, 0, 0, 274, 0, 0, 1024, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 58162),
('', 'O-okay.', 270795, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 1024, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 58162),
('', 'I thought I had her removed!', 270779, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 1024, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 58162),
('', 'Is that Ellie? The cat from the Dauntless?', 270778, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 1024, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 58162),
('<Gazix lets out a long sigh.>\n\nLook, I know us goblins aren\'t known for being environmentally conscious, but Gazlowe\'s been workin\' real hard on improvin\' our image. \n\nAnd I, for one, don\'t like livin\' in garbage, so it\'s a win-win.', '', 270764, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 1024, 0, 0, 256, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 58162),
('<Gazix gives you a grateful smile.>\n\nThanks kid.', '', 270759, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 1024, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 58162),
('<Gazix raises a long, bushy eyebrow at you.>\n\nCleanin\'! What\'s it look like I\'m doin\'?\n\nWhat, you ain\'t ever seen a goblin pickin\' up garbage before?', '', 270754, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 1024, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 58162),
('Can I help you with somethin\'?', '', 270711, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 1024, 0, 0, 60672, 3, 0, 0, 0, 0, 58162),
('', 'I will dispose of the bomb. Destroy the other artifacts and meet me in the Tranquil Strand.', 270710, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 1024, 0, 68673536, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 58162),
('', 'This bomb should not have been built. Kirin Tor leadership is to blame. But we are all complicit and must atone for it.', 270709, 0, 0, 669, 0, 0, 1792, 0, 68691456, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 58162),
('', 'But my visions have put me on another path. I was told your people share these visions.', 270688, 0, 0, 1, 0, 0, 1024, 0, 68604928, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 58162),
('The surprises never end. Meet you both back at Opportunity Point.', '', 270687, 0, 0, 1, 0, 0, 1024, 68594688, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 58162),
('Come, Kai\'shae, let us get back to the others and see to your wounds.', '', 270686, 0, 0, 1, 0, 0, 1024, 68563200, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 58162);

INSERT INTO `broadcast_text` (`Text`, `Text1`, `ID`, `LanguageID`, `ConditionID`, `EmotesID`, `Flags`, `ChatBubbleDurationMs`, `VoiceOverPriorityID`, `SoundKitID1`, `SoundKitID2`, `EmoteID1`, `EmoteID2`, `EmoteID3`, `EmoteDelay1`, `EmoteDelay2`, `EmoteDelay3`, `VerifiedBuild`) VALUES
('', 'Even now it lingers in Hallowfall, long after our last battle. Please investigate it further.', 270685, 0, 0, 1, 0, 0, 1024, 0, 68556544, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 58162),
('', 'There\'s a lot less sneezing, itching, and runny noses. Once, my fingers swelled up so much they looked like sausages!', 270612, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 1024, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 58162),
('', 'I approve of mechanical cats, $n. But only mechanical cats.', 270611, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 1024, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 58162),
('', 'You truly test my patience $n.', 270610, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 1024, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 58162),
('', 'An Imperial Lynx?', 270609, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 1024, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 58162),
('', 'My allergies will not tolerate its presence!', 270608, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 1024, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 58162),
('', 'Is that $r riding a cat?', 270607, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 1024, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 58162),
('', 'Now, $n! Realign the mana bomb\'s matrix!', 270589, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 2048, 0, 68682752, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 58162),
('', 'There\'s so many forests in da panda land!\n\nI fink I saw some spoopy crawly animals near a pretty lake in the Jade Forest.\n\nFor the second riddle, try looking reeaaaally high up in the snowy area.', 270436, 0, 0, 1, 0, 0, 1024, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 58162),
('', 'I will scout on my own. Good luck with your hunt.', 270426, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 1024, 0, 68587264, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 58162),
('And that\'s what\'s happening. Gallywix is back in business, and that ain\'t good for no one.', '', 270396, 0, 0, 1, 0, 0, 1024, 68604160, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 58162),
('', 'Closure is finding peace in saying goodbye.', 269860, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 1024, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 58162),
('', 'Disentangle the bomb\'s power sources while I suppress it. We cannot allow the mana bomb to detonate!', 269793, 0, 0, 669, 0, 0, 2048, 0, 68663552, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 58162),
('Kinda busy here provin\' myself in-dis-put-ably correct!\n\nYou can handle your problems on your own, right? \n\nGreat, champ. I owe ya one!', '', 269397, 0, 0, 5, 0, 0, 1024, 0, 0, 1280, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 58162),
('', 'Grab any equipment that might help ya. I\'m just gonna go hide over here.', 269258, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 1024, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 58162),
('', 'This is far worse than I expected!', 269257, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 1024, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 58162),
('', 'Smart money says to run when a storm rolls in!\n\nBut I\'ve never been good with money, so I\'ll probably stick around and see what happens!', 269240, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 1024, 0, 0, 256, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 58162),
('', 'No one will be blown up by cannons or ground to pieces by a drill bit.', 269168, 0, 0, 5, 0, 0, 1024, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 58162),
('', 'Our kobold assistants can meticulously excavate the cave.', 269159, 0, 0, 5, 0, 0, 1024, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 58162),
('', 'Perhaps a more cautious approach is wise?', 269158, 0, 0, 5, 0, 0, 1024, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 58162),
('A couple of my best goblins, some explosives--we\'ll crack this island open and take everything!', '', 269157, 0, 0, 5, 0, 0, 1024, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 58162),
('We don\'t need any flying boats for my plan!', '', 269156, 0, 0, 14, 0, 0, 1024, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 58162),
('', 'Rest assured, the might of my airship guarantees the success of my plan!', 269155, 0, 0, 1, 0, 0, 1024, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 58162),
('', 'We have averted a great catastrophe, $n.', 268502, 0, 0, 669, 0, 0, 1024, 0, 68693504, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 58162),
('', 'I just realized I\'m afraid of heights.', 268432, 0, 0, 1, 0, 0, 1024, 0, 68597760, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 58162),
('Hardly workin\', definitely.', '', 268431, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 1024, 68597504, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 58162),
('The real opportunity is on the other side of that wall.', '', 268430, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 1024, 68597248, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 58162),
('', 'Oh man, I\'ve got all my money tied up in this venture! Ugh, no! Not that Venture, are you crazy?', 268429, 0, 0, 1, 0, 0, 1024, 0, 68596992, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 58162),
('I\'m off the clock Bilgewater. I am here lookin\' out for goblin interests.', '', 268426, 0, 0, 1, 0, 0, 1024, 68595200, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 58162),
('No mooks allowed! Not even with a work permit!', '', 267559, 0, 0, 1, 0, 0, 1024, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 58162),
('Fancy meeting you out here.', '', 267534, 0, 0, 1, 0, 0, 1024, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 58162),
('You are not alone, friends.', '', 267509, 0, 0, 1, 68, 0, 1024, 68697088, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 58162),
('Huh, interesting. Eh, keep asking around, and I\'ll do the same. Keep your eyes open.', '', 267497, 0, 0, 1, 0, 0, 1024, 68587520, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 58162),
('Look, they promised if I could figure out how to get this all going, I would get promoted to foreman!', 'Look, they promised if I could figure out how to get this all going, I would get promoted to foreman!', 267467, 0, 0, 1, 0, 0, 1024, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 58162),
('I was the top of my class when it comes to mechanical innovation. And this is not what I expected.', 'I was the top of my class when it comes to mechanical innovation. And this is not what I expected.', 267466, 0, 0, 1, 0, 0, 1024, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 58162),
('Between you and me, I\'m just here until overtime kicks in. But I\'m starting to reconsider.', 'Between you and me, I\'m just here until overtime kicks in. But I\'m starting to reconsider.', 267465, 0, 0, 1, 0, 0, 1024, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 58162),
('This ain\'t worth it! I didn\'t sign up for crazy machines.', 'This ain\'t worth it! I didn\'t sign up for crazy machines.', 267464, 0, 0, 1, 0, 0, 1024, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 58162),
('You\'ll never get to meet the big boss...', '', 267451, 0, 0, 5, 0, 0, 1024, 68586496, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 58162),
('Back off! This job is mine! I paid good bribes for it!', '', 267450, 0, 0, 5, 0, 0, 1024, 68586240, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 58162),
('There you are. Did you get that permit?', '', 267449, 0, 0, 6, 0, 0, 1024, 68586752, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 58162),
('There are things that are more important than this mission. We must take care of each other, even if it means leaving some questions unanswered.\n\nWe have been through too much for what we have achieved.', '', 267338, 0, 0, 1, 0, 0, 1024, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 58162),
('', 'I know we are close to answers. I cannot stop now.', 267337, 0, 0, 1, 0, 0, 1024, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 58162),
('Kai\'shae needs real healing. We must return to our homeland for proper rest.', '', 267267, 0, 0, 1, 0, 0, 1024, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 58162),
('<On\'hiea glares through rivulets of blood flowing down his face.>', '', 267266, 0, 0, 1, 0, 0, 1024, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 58162),
('', 'I haven\'t slept well in ages. How can I be at my full abilities if we\'re never stopping to rest?', 267261, 0, 0, 1, 0, 0, 1024, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 58162),
('', 'If you want to talk about visions, I know just the dwarf.', 267132, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 1024, 0, 68605184, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 58162),
('', 'That is our way... it was my way.', 267131, 0, 0, 1, 0, 0, 1024, 0, 68604672, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 58162),
('', 'Our mysterious ally returns. You slipped away last time, before we could thank you.', 267130, 0, 0, 1, 0, 0, 1024, 0, 68604416, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 58162),
('I\'m going to keep looking for the source of those sounds. And Bilgewater, don\'t forget about your people while you\'re off saving the world.', '', 267128, 0, 0, 1, 0, 0, 1024, 68603648, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 58162),
('', 'Friends...', 267127, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 1024, 0, 68603392, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 58162),
('Looks like we\'re on the same path. Join us on the surface and maybe you can get some help from your new friends.', '', 267124, 0, 0, 1, 0, 0, 1024, 68603136, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 58162),
('', 'I must follow my visions, follow this calling, until I have found what the goddess wants me to see.', 267122, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 1024, 0, 68602880, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 58162),
('You\'ve been hiding under the Horde\'s skirts too long. Gallywix is back, making deals, and making trouble. Things have changed.', '', 267121, 0, 0, 1, 0, 0, 1024, 68600064, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 58162),
('Gallywix! Without the Bilgewater Cartel, he shouldn\'t have the resources for an operation here.', '', 267120, 0, 0, 5, 0, 0, 1024, 68599296, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 58162),
('', 'While you fought the machine, I witnessed something inside.', 267119, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 1024, 0, 68599040, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 58162),
('', 'Next I went searching for you, $n. I found you outside the building.', 267118, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 1024, 0, 68598784, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 58162),
('Sounds like a rocket drill, a big one. But who\'s running it?', '', 267117, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 1024, 68598528, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 58162),
('', 'It sounded like the earth ground itself to nothing. What manner of machine does this?', 267116, 0, 0, 1, 0, 0, 1024, 0, 68598272, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 58162),
('', 'I saw little of use when observing the other goblins, but I heard things coming from the wall.', 267115, 0, 0, 1, 0, 0, 1024, 0, 68598016, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 58162),
('Spill it, Renzik. What\'s an SI:7 agent doin\' down here?', '', 267112, 0, 0, 1, 0, 0, 1024, 68594944, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 58162),
('She\'s got the goods, Monte. She was flying around all over the place.', '', 267106, 0, 0, 5, 0, 0, 1024, 68589568, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 58162),
('', 'There is no going back now. Small green one, I propose an exchange of information.', 267105, 0, 0, 1, 0, 0, 1024, 0, 68589056, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 58162),
('Uhhh, what? Who are you? What are you?', '', 267104, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 1024, 68588800, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 58162),
('', 'Die, foul machine!', 267102, 0, 0, 22, 0, 0, 1024, 0, 68588544, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 58162),
('A little help? Kind of bit off more than I can chew!', '', 267101, 0, 0, 1, 0, 0, 1024, 68588288, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 58162),
('No one\'s going anywhere while that massive boom-bot is running amok. Take it out, and we\'ll talk. Deal?', '', 267100, 0, 0, 1, 0, 0, 1024, 68588032, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 58162),
('Psst! You\'re like an ogre in Gnomeregan, asking questions and breaking things. Get over here.', '', 267099, 0, 0, 1, 0, 0, 1024, 68587776, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 58162),
('If you really want to know what\'s going on... The foreman keeps all the orders in his office.', '', 267098, 0, 0, 1, 0, 0, 1024, 68860672, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 58162),
('', 'That new fuel is causing all sorts of problems. We didn\'t get hazard pay for experiments!', 267097, 0, 0, 5, 0, 0, 1024, 0, 68860416, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 58162),
('', 'I wanted less work for more pay, instead I got busted machines and overtime! Who runs a site like this?', 267096, 0, 0, 5, 0, 0, 1024, 0, 68860160, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 58162),
('You want to know what the drilling\'s about? Buddy, it\'s bigger than you can imagine!', '', 267095, 0, 0, 1, 0, 0, 1024, 68859904, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 58162),
('Keep an eye out for anything odd while you ask around. There\'s more here than they\'re letting on.', '', 267094, 0, 0, 1, 0, 0, 1024, 68587008, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 58162),
('This Haxle guy has the papers we need to set up close and see what they\'re up to.', '', 267092, 0, 0, 1, 0, 0, 1024, 68585728, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 58162),
('', 'Go. I will follow unseen. This must be what the visions meant for us to do.', 267090, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 1024, 0, 68585984, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 58162),
('Hey, $p! Nice timing. We got trouble brewing.', '', 267089, 0, 0, 1, 0, 0, 1024, 68577536, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 58162),
('Get lost, you lump of rock! These items are now the property of Opportunity Acquisitions. Where we acquire at every opportunity!', '', 267088, 0, 0, 1, 0, 0, 1024, 68580864, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 58162),
('', 'Look for me in another form. At least I can honor one haranir tradition.', 267086, 0, 0, 1, 0, 0, 1024, 0, 68577280, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 58162),
('', 'The vision-- we are close. But I must remain unseen by the people there.', 267085, 0, 0, 1, 0, 0, 1024, 0, 68576256, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 58162),
('', 'I do not understand what you want me to see.', 267084, 0, 0, 1, 0, 0, 1024, 0, 68575744, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 58162),
('', 'I hear the drumming? No... the ringing, striking and thunder from solid rock...', 267083, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 1024, 0, 68575488, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 58162),
('', 'Goddess, grant me a vision of what I must do.', 267082, 0, 0, 1, 0, 0, 1024, 0, 68575232, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 58162),
('', 'I cannot do this alone. Your aid is the only reason I can continue.', 267081, 0, 0, 1, 0, 0, 1024, 0, 68574976, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 58162),
('', 'I must press on. I must. If I do not, the Black Blood may consume all that I care about.', 267080, 0, 0, 1, 0, 0, 1024, 0, 68574720, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 58162),
('Continue? Orweyna, we must retreat and speak.', '', 267078, 0, 0, 1, 0, 0, 1024, 68574464, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 58162),
('', 'You are safe. Come, we must recover before continuing our fight.', 267077, 0, 0, 1, 0, 0, 1024, 0, 68574208, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 58162),
('I have had enough of this.', '', 267076, 0, 0, 1, 0, 0, 1024, 68562944, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 58162),
('We have too many injuries. We cannot last much longer.', '', 267075, 0, 0, 1, 0, 0, 1024, 68562176, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 58162),
('', 'This time, she\'s gone too far. Why won\'t she see that she will chase these visions forever?', 267074, 0, 0, 1, 0, 0, 1024, 0, 68562688, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 58162),
('', 'And help has arrived. We can still see this through.', 267073, 0, 0, 1, 0, 0, 1024, 0, 68573952, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 58162),
('This is not the time for visions, Orweyna! Our people need help right now.', '', 267071, 0, 0, 1, 0, 0, 1024, 68573696, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 58162),
('', 'Do not lose hope, Hannan! They will be safe. I have seen it!', 267066, 0, 0, 5, 0, 0, 1024, 0, 68561920, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 58162),
('', 'Xal\'atath has been forced to retreat, but she and the Black Blood are still out there.', 267065, 0, 0, 1, 0, 0, 1024, 0, 68556288, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 58162),
('What if all of us--even Archaedas himself--have been deceived?', '', 265601, 0, 0, 0, 100, 0, 1024, 64539136, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 58162),
('I\'m starting to think there\'s more to the Worldsoul than the titans wanted us to know. That they had other plans for it-- and Azeroth--than we were led to believe.', '', 265600, 0, 0, 0, 100, 0, 1024, 64538880, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 58162),
('', 'Our entire history--our culture--held in that Archive... I want my memories back. I want ALL our memories back. Damn the titans.', 265598, 0, 0, 0, 100, 0, 1024, 0, 64538624, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 58162),
('', 'And then when the Sundering happened, we were cut off from all of it--and Archaedas never returned to help us. Why didn\'t he return?', 265597, 0, 0, 0, 100, 0, 1024, 0, 64538368, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 58162),
('', 'Those Edicts... they were bonds of servitude. And we never even knew.', 265596, 0, 0, 0, 100, 0, 1024, 0, 64538112, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 58162),
('And it does seem that they did it to keep you complacent... obedient. Following their Edicts--and eliminating those of you they couldn\'t control.', '', 265595, 0, 0, 0, 100, 0, 1024, 64537856, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 58162),
('', 'We built the greatest structures the world has ever seen, and they set us to become... maintenance drones, just... cogs in a machine.', 265594, 0, 0, 0, 100, 0, 1024, 0, 64537600, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 58162),
('', 'So the keepers stole our memories, and let us believe that it was for our own good? That it was so we could continue to fulfill our purpose--no, not even our purpose!', 265593, 0, 0, 0, 100, 0, 1024, 0, 64537344, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 58162),
('What we\'ve learned here... It calls the entire history of Azeroth into question. What if... what if our history isn\'t what they said it was?', '', 265592, 0, 0, 0, 100, 0, 1024, 64537088, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 58162),
('I do not know why I commit this information to the Archive--why I risk its discovery in the future. Perhaps the Worldsoul\'s influence does not extend solely to the earthen.', '', 265591, 0, 0, 0, 100, 0, 1024, 64536832, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 58162),
('With these difficulties behind them, the titans have declared that the Worldsoul remains, dreaming, safely contained within the Worldcore, where no harm will come to it.', '', 265590, 0, 0, 0, 100, 0, 1024, 64536576, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 58162),
('Thus, the earthen will maintain the integrity of the Coreway and the machines of Khaz Algar. Should the Edicts be broken, more permanent failsafes have been set into place.', '', 265584, 0, 0, 0, 100, 0, 1024, 64536320, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 58162),
('To secure compliance, the titans have programmed Edicts into the operational earthen to regulate and enforce their discreet functions and efficiency.', '', 265583, 0, 0, 0, 100, 0, 1024, 64536064, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 58162),
('By initiating this protocol on a regular cadence, we will ensure the thraegar malfunction does not take hold again.', '', 265582, 0, 0, 0, 100, 0, 1024, 64535808, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 58162),
('The earthen of Khaz Algar will relinquish their memories into an Archive to preserve recorded data, and purge the influence of the Worldsoul\'s energies.', '', 265581, 0, 0, 0, 100, 0, 1024, 64535552, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 58162),
('However, the issue of earthen malfunction under the influence of the Worldsoul\'s energies remained, and so a new solution was devised.', '', 265580, 0, 0, 0, 100, 0, 1024, 64535296, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 58162),
('With the danger posed by the rogue thraegar, the great Aman\'Thul ordered the rebellion to be quelled and the thraegar hunted down until the threat was neutralized.', '', 265573, 0, 0, 0, 100, 0, 1024, 64535040, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 58162),
('', 'Well done. Looking forward to seeing the images you captured.', 263949, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 1024, 0, 64601344, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 58162),
('', 'The Cataract River is known for its wildlife and waterfalls. Can you use your camera to document the region? Appreciation expressed.', 263948, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 1024, 0, 64602112, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 58162),
('Wow really? It\'s a pretty hard course. Only the very best can make it!\n\nIf you do it, we\'ll be super impressed!', 'Wow really? It\'s a pretty hard course. Only the very best can make it!\n\nIf you do it, we\'ll be super impressed!', 263820, 0, 0, 1, 0, 0, 1024, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 58162),
('', 'I can hear their laughter already. Thank you, $n.', 263818, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 1024, 0, 64358656, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 58162),
('', 'The orphans of Mereldar have been asking to play with you again. I think they\'d appreciate it if you visited them.', 263817, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 1024, 0, 64358400, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 58162),
('', 'Well done. We\'re in a much stronger position if we only need to defend the breach.', 263698, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 1024, 0, 64355584, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 58162),
('', 'Nerubians are still tunneling under the wall. The people of Hallowfall aren\'t safe until those burrows are collapsed.', 263697, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 1024, 0, 64355328, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 58162),
('Are you sure? Wyllam is the best at hiding, but he\'s hard to find.\n\nIf you find him, we\'ll be super impressed!', 'Are you sure? Wyllam is the best at hiding, but he\'s hard to find.\n\nIf you find him, we\'ll be super impressed!', 263626, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 1024, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 58162),
('$n! Welcome, come in, please!\n\nAre you here to help? You\'ve really been making a difference!', '', 262195, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 1024, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 58162),
('We\'re making good progress. Your help has been invaluable, $n.\n\nIt\'s been a long time since we\'ve had empty beds in here. We still have injured coming in every day, but at least we are getting them back out faster.\n\nThe more people out there helping, the better.', '', 256945, 0, 0, 1, 0, 0, 1024, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 58162),
('My family is whole again... as is my soul. I cannot thank you enough, champions.', '', 245265, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 1024, 59187200, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 58162),
('It is done. The Headless Horseman is no more.', '', 245263, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 1024, 59186944, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 58162),
('Come forth my minions, unleash your breath! Choke them with the stench of death!', '', 245262, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 1024, 59187456, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 58162);

